{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#81508765-6076-4478-ab3e-cb1a6331a8e2","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"81508765-6076-4478-ab3e-cb1a6331a8e2","dateCreated":"2026-09-22T21:12:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-09-22T21:44:48+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Route 53 Resolver is now generally available on second-generation AWS Outposts, providing local, managed recursive DNS resolution directly on your Outpost. DNS queries from workloads running on your Outpost are resolved locally, reducing latency and eliminating the need to traverse the Service Link to reach the parent AWS Region. Route 53 Resolver maintains cached DNS records during Service Link disconnections, ensuring continuous DNS resolution even during connectivity interruptions. Route 53 Resolver runs entirely on AWS-managed infrastructure built into every second-generation Outpost, eliminating the need for customer compute capacity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoute 53 Resolver is enabled by default on multi-rack second-generation Outposts. Customers who prefer to manage their own DNS resolution can opt out at any time by contacting AWS Support.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoute 53 Resolver on second-generation Outposts is available in all AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts are supported. All customers, including current preview customers, receive a 91-day free trial through December 21, 2026. Starting December 22, 2026, the service is priced at $0.65 per Outpost rack per hour. To get started, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/outpost-resolver.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eRoute 53 Resolver on Outposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e. For pricing details, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/route53/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAmazon Route 53 pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/route-53-resolver-gen2-outposts/","postDateTime":"2026-09-22T08:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Route 53 Resolver is now generally available on second-generation AWS Outposts racks"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-route-53","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-route-53","description":"general:products/amazon-route-53","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-5m18uint6pdvy3je1mmdxf","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-5m18uint6pdvy3je1mmdxf","dateCreated":"2026-09-08T17:58:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-09-10T18:08:03+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces the general availability of second-generation single-rack AWS Outposts, a self-contained 42U rack that integrates compute, storage and networking into a single compact unit purpose-built for workloads requiring low latency, local data processing, and data residency in space and power constrained locations. A single-rack Outposts delivers up to 2,688 vCPU and 100 TB of Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) storage. Moreover, like multi-rack Outposts, single-rack Outposts support the latest x86-powered EC2 instances, including general purpose (M7i, M8i), compute-optimized (C7i, C8i), memory-optimized (R7i, R8i), and Outposts accelerated networking (Bmn-sf2e, Bmn-cx2, Bmn-cx3a) instances.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor organizations that operate in locations with limited rack space, such as manufacturing, gaming, and other industries, single-rack Outposts brings the latest AWS compute, storage, and networking features on-premises, and gives customers a direct path to modernize while leveraging their currently available space and power. Single-rack and multi-rack Outposts offer customers a consistent experience with the same AWS APIs, management console, automation, governance policies, and security controls across AWS Regions and on-premises locations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a current list of AWS Regions and countries/territories where Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-is-outposts-rack-available-trigger\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, open the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eAWS Outposts console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/single-rack-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2026-09-10T17:58:00Z","headline":"Announcing second-generation single-rack AWS Outposts "}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-igtey24zzh3d9ecbsm1hhx-1","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-igtey24zzh3d9ecbsm1hhx-1","dateCreated":"2026-09-02T18:39:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-09-02T18:39:34+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","nosnippet":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West) Regions. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector can now order their Outposts racks connected to the new supported regions, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-outposts-govcloud-us-regions/","postDateTime":"2026-09-02T16:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks now in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#a1d95d6a-ec76-4bf9-a0b4-d3c3b852a4f7","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"a1d95d6a-ec76-4bf9-a0b4-d3c3b852a4f7","dateCreated":"2026-07-23T20:48:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-07-28T16:34:18+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","nosnippet":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the Asia Pacific (Mumbai) Region. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of India can now order their Outposts racks connected to this new supported region, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/aws-outposts-asia-pacific-mumbai/","postDateTime":"2026-07-28T16:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks now supported in the AWS Asia Pacific (Mumbai) Region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-5xjh2xqxsy2udahnwxw1xb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-5xjh2xqxsy2udahnwxw1xb","dateCreated":"2026-04-22T23:43:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-04-23T18:30:54+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the AWS Asia Pacific (Seoul, Sydney) and Europe (Paris) Regions. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of South Korea, Australia, and France can now order their Outposts racks connected to this new supported region, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/04/second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-sydney-seoul-paris/","postDateTime":"2026-04-23T16:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks now supported in the AWS Asia Pacific (Seoul, Sydney) and Europe (Paris) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-qipjlyeno25h93uztjsahz","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-qipjlyeno25h93uztjsahz","dateCreated":"2026-02-25T21:34:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-03-31T17:09:35+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts racks now support VifConnectionStatus and VifBgpSessionState Amazon CloudWatch metrics in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. These metrics provide visibility into the connectivity status of your Outposts racks\u0027 Local Gateway (LGW) and Service Link Virtual Interfaces (VIFs) with your on-premises devices.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThese metrics provide you with the ability to monitor Outposts VIF connectivity status directly within the CloudWatch console, without having to rely on external networking tools or coordination with other teams. You can use these metrics to set alarms, troubleshoot connectivity issues, and ensure your Outposts racks are properly integrated with your on-premises infrastructure. The VifConnectionStatus metric indicates whether an Outposts VIF is successfully connected, configured, and ready to forward traffic. A value of \u0026quot;1\u0026quot; means that the VIF is operational, while \u0026quot;0\u0026quot; means that it is not ready. The VifBgpSessionState metric shows the current state of the BGP session between the Outposts VIF and the on-premises device, with values ranging from 1 (IDLE) to 6 (ESTABLISHED).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThe VifConnectionStatus and VifBgpSessionState metrics are now available for all Outposts VIFs in AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West) Regions where Outposts racks are available.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo get started, read this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/improving-network-observability-with-new-aws-outposts-racks-network-metrics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eblog post \u003c/a\u003eand access the metrics in the CloudWatch console. To learn more, check out the CloudWatch metrics for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-cloudwatch-metrics.html#metrics-vif\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eOutposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e for first-generation Outposts racks.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/aws-outposts-racks-cloudwatch-metrics-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2026-02-25T21:30:00Z","headline":"AWS Outposts racks now support additional Amazon CloudWatch metrics in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#local-tags-whats-new-v2-general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#local-tags-whats-new-v2-general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-06-30T19:51:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-06-30T19:51:30+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-6p68ghmuu5jureqkk2znau","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-6p68ghmuu5jureqkk2znau","dateCreated":"2026-02-12T22:36:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-02-13T00:41:32+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS is announcing local support for the latest generation of x86-powered Amazon EC2 instances on second-generation AWS Outposts racks, including C8i compute-optimized instances, M8i general-purpose instances, and R8i memory-optimized instances. These new instances deliver 20% better performance and 2.5x more memory bandwidth compared to the C7i, M7i, and R7i instances on second-generation Outposts racks. In addition, C8i, M8i, and R8i instances on second-generation Outposts racks deliver 20% more compute capacity than C7i, M7i, and R7i instances within the same rack space and power draw, enabling better space and energy efficiency for your on-premises workloads.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nC8i, M8i, and R8i instances on second-generation Outposts racks are powered by custom Intel Xeon 6 processors available only on AWS and are ideal for a broad range of on-premises workloads requiring enhanced performance, such as larger databases, more memory-intensive applications, advanced real-time big data analytics, high-performance video encoding and streaming, and CPU-based edge inference with more sophisticated machine learning (ML) models.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, refer to the Outposts racks \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eproduct page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cu\u003e \u003c/u\u003eand the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-ec2-c8i-m8i-and-r8i-instances-on-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2026-02-12T22:34:00Z","headline":"Announcing Amazon EC2 C8i, M8i, and R8i instances on second-generation AWS Outposts racks"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-khjmpehrewnvt1p4c9usip","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-khjmpehrewnvt1p4c9usip","dateCreated":"2026-01-22T22:30:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-01-22T22:57:14+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts racks can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Rwanda.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts racks allow customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to a home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts racks to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Outposts racks, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"about-aws/whats-new/2026/01/availability-aws-outposts-racks-rwanda","postDateTime":"2026-01-22T16:00:00Z","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts racks in Rwanda"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-f75sivhe35bj7uubmwrpcx","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-f75sivhe35bj7uubmwrpcx","dateCreated":"2026-01-07T19:36:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-01-21T23:44:48+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Argentina, Bangladesh, Colombia, Dominican Republic, Ecuador, India, Kazakhstan, Mexico, Morocco, Nigeria, Oman, Panama, Qatar, Senegal, Serbia, South Africa, Republic of Korea, Taiwan, Thailand, and Uruguay.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOutposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts racks are ideal for workloads requiring low-latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, data residency compliance, and migration of applications with local system dependencies. Second-generation Outposts racks support the latest generation of x86-powered Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances, starting with C7i, M7i, and R7i instances. These instances provide up to 40% better performance compared to C5, M5, and R5 instances on first-generation Outposts racks. Second-generation Outposts racks also offer simplified network scaling and configuration, and support a new category of accelerated networking Amazon EC2 instances optimized for ultra-low latency and high throughput needs.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nWith the availability of second-generation Outposts racks in the above countries, you can run AWS services locally in your on-premises facilities to maintain data residency within your country, while connecting to a supported AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\"\u003ethis blog post\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/01/availability-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-more-countries","postDateTime":"2026-01-21T15:00:00Z","headline":"Announcing availability of second-generation AWS Outposts racks in 20 more countries"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-ga7estbdjzpakldjpcg579","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-ga7estbdjzpakldjpcg579","dateCreated":"2026-01-07T19:06:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-01-16T18:18:18+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the South America (Sao Paulo) and Europe (Stockholm) Regions. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of Europe and South America can now order their Outposts racks connected to these new supported regions, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/01/second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-additional-aws-regions","postDateTime":"2026-01-16T15:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in additional AWS Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#1i83drlgvfdhsvixfa1ixv","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"1i83drlgvfdhsvixfa1ixv","dateCreated":"2026-01-15T20:26:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-01-15T23:41:05+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts is now available on second-generation AWS Outposts racks for your data residency, low latency, and local data processing use cases on-premises. S3 on Outposts on second-generation Outposts racks offers three storage tiers: 196 TB, 490 TB, and 786 TB. Choose the storage tier that matches your workload, whether for production workloads, backups, or archival workloads.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nWith S3 on Outposts, you can store, secure, retrieve, and control access to your data using familiar S3 APIs and features. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nS3 on Outposts on second-generation Outposts racks is available in all AWS Regions and countries/territories where these \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eracks are available\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/01/amazon-s3-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks","postDateTime":"2026-01-15T20:23:00Z","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts is now available on second-generation AWS Outposts racks"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-jhkac4bgqsnjfh6dtm1cja","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-jhkac4bgqsnjfh6dtm1cja","dateCreated":"2025-11-20T14:53:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-11-21T18:37:34+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the AWS Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Region. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of Japan can now order their Outposts racks connected to this new supported region, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-asia-pacific-tokyo-region","postDateTime":"2025-11-21T18:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks now supported in the AWS Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-tvdtzicgvxwrxcowsibnhi","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-tvdtzicgvxwrxcowsibnhi","dateCreated":"2025-10-20T23:16:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-10-31T20:47:08+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts 2U server is now supported in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West) Regions. Outposts 2U server is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to on-premises or edge locations with limited space or smaller capacity requirements for a truly consistent hybrid experience. It is delivered in an industry-standard 2U form factor and provides up to 128 vCPUs of compute. It is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency and stringent compliance requirements. You can also use Outposts 2U server to manage your local data processing needs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts 2U server in the GovCloud (US-East) and GovCloud (US-West) Regions, you can now run Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2), Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), and AWS IoT Greengrass locally on Outposts 2U servers, and connect to a broader range of AWS services available in the parent AWS GovCloud (US) Region. For AWS GovCloud (US) Regions customers, this means you can run sensitive and controlled unclassified information (CUI) data on-premises at your facilities and connect to the parent AWS GovCloud (US) Region for management and operations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts 2U server, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/server-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/10/aws-outposts-2u-server-govcloud-regions","postDateTime":"2025-10-23T16:00:00Z","headline":"AWS Outposts 2U server is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-tbv2gfw9gxrhajl6witcqg","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-tbv2gfw9gxrhajl6witcqg","dateCreated":"2025-10-10T15:43:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-10-15T18:01:32+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the AWS Europe (Ireland) Region. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of Europe can now order their Outposts racks connected to this new supported region, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/10/second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-europe-ireland-region","postDateTime":"2025-10-15T14:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks now supported in the AWS Europe (Ireland) Region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-f37cvxx4swv7nvdjxcazqf","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-f37cvxx4swv7nvdjxcazqf","dateCreated":"2025-09-26T18:48:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-30T17:11:40+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use boot and data volumes backed by Dell PowerStore and HPE Alletra Storage MP B10000 storage arrays with Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances on AWS Outposts, including authenticated and encrypted volumes. This enhancement extends our existing support for boot and data volumes to include Dell and HPE storage arrays, alongside our current support for NetApp® on-premises enterprise storage arrays and Pure Storage® FlashArray™. Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nWith Outposts, customers can maximize the value of their on-premises storage investments by leveraging their existing enterprise storage arrays for both boot and data volumes, complementing managed Amazon EBS and Local Instance Store options. This provides significant operational benefits, including streamlined operating system (OS) management via centralized boot volumes and advanced data management features through high-performance data volumes. By integrating their own storage, organizations can also satisfy data residency requirements and benefit from a consistent cloud operational model for their hybrid environments.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo simplify the process, AWS offers automation scripts through AWS Samples to help customers easily set up and use external block volumes with EC2 instances on Outposts. Customers can use the AWS Management Console or CLI to utilize third-party block volumes with EC2 instances on Outposts.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThird-party storage integration for Outposts with all compatible storage vendors is available on Outposts 2U servers and Outposts racks at no additional charge in all AWS Regions where Outposts is supported. See the FAQs for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/?nc\u003dsn\u0026amp;loc\u003d4\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts racks\u003c/a\u003e for the latest list of supported Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about implementation details and best practices, check out \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/deploying-external-boot-volumes-with-aws-outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis blog post\u003c/a\u003e or visit our technical documentation for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/server-userguide/outpost-third-party-block-storage.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/outpost-third-party-block-storage.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esecond-generation Outposts racks\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outpost-third-party-block-storage.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003efirst-generation Outposts racks\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/aws-outposts-external-block-volumes-dell-hpe-storage-arrays","postDateTime":"2025-09-30T14:00:00Z","headline":"AWS Outposts now supports external block volumes from Dell and HPE storage arrays"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-phfvbqhurxbrwp9vtgxzzr","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-phfvbqhurxbrwp9vtgxzzr","dateCreated":"2025-09-18T18:08:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-18T18:31:33+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks are now supported in the AWS Canada (Central) and US West (N. California) Regions. Outposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of Canada and the US can now order their Outposts racks connected to these two new supported Regions, optimizing for their latency and data residency needs. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low-latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003ethis blog post\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003euser guide\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eOutposts racks FAQs page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/second-generation-outposts-racks-canada-us-west-regions","postDateTime":"2025-09-18T17:00:00Z","headline":"Second-generation AWS Outposts racks now supported in the AWS Canada (Central) and US West (N. California) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-fjhp7nohygsukofuk1w47i","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-fjhp7nohygsukofuk1w47i","dateCreated":"2025-08-15T00:56:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-17T20:14:40+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation AWS Outposts racks can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Australia, Bahrain, Brazil, Brunei, Chile, Costa Rica, Egypt, European Union countries, Iceland, Indonesia, Israel, Japan, Jordan, Kenya, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Malaysia, New Zealand, Peru, the Philippines, Singapore, Trinidad and Tobago, Türkiye, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), the United Kingdom, and Vietnam.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOutposts racks extend AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts racks are ideal for workloads that require low-latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts racks can also help meet data residency requirements. Second-generation Outposts racks support the latest generation of x86-powered Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances, starting with C7i, M7i, and R7i instances. These instances provide up to 40% better performance compared to C5, M5, and R5 instances on first-generation Outposts racks. Second-generation Outposts racks also offer simplified network scaling and configuration, and support a new category of accelerated networking Amazon EC2 instances optimized for ultra-low latency and high throughput needs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of second-generation Outposts racks in the above countries, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to the nearest available AWS Region for management and operations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about second-generation Outposts racks, read \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis blog post\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/network-userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories and the AWS Regions where second-generation Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts racks FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-more-countries","postDateTime":"2025-09-17T16:00:00Z","headline":"Announcing availability of second-generation AWS Outposts racks in 52 more countries"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1820535521","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-pr9EkkAoxGRBAwxm59Q3t4","dateCreated":"2025-06-27T17:59:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-06-30T18:49:15+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use Amazon EBS General Purpose SSD volumes (gp3) volumes with the second-generation AWS Outposts racks for your workloads that require local data processing and data residency. The latest generation of gp3 enables you to provision performance independently of storage capacity, delivering a baseline performance of 3,000 IOPS and 125 MB/s at any volume size. With gp3 volumes, you can scale up to 16,000 IOPS and 1,000 MB/s, delivering 4x the maximum throughput of the previously supported gp2 volumes.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nEBS gp3 volumes on second-generation AWS Outposts are ideal for a wide variety of performance-intensive applications, including MySQL, Cassandra, virtual desktops, and Hadoop analytics clusters. AWS Outposts racks offer the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or colocation space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Second-generation AWS Outposts racks support the latest generation of x86-powered Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances, starting with C7i, M7i, and R7i instances. These instances deliver twice the vCPU, memory, and network bandwidth, as well as up to 40% better performance compared to C5, M5, and R5 instances on first-generation AWS Outposts racks.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nYou can manage gp3 volumes using the AWS Management Console, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), or the AWS SDKs in all Regions and countries/territories where second-generation\u003cstrong\u003e \u003c/strong\u003eAWS Outposts racks are supported. For more information on gp3 volumes, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ebs/volume-types/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cu\u003eproduct overview page\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. For a current list of AWS Regions and countries/territories where second-generation AWS Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-is-outposts-rack-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts racks FAQs page.\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/06/amazon-ebs-gp3-volumes-second-generation-outposts-racks/","postDateTime":"2025-06-30T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Announcing Amazon EBS gp3 volumes for second-generation AWS Outposts racks"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-block-store","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-block-store","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-block-store","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launchmarketingintake-1361","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"i6dSDzHRQKeFjRx7QifqXn","dateCreated":"2025-04-24T18:57:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-04-29T20:14:08+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces the general availability of second-generation AWS Outposts racks, marking the latest innovation from AWS at the edge of the cloud for your workloads that require low latency, local data processing, and data residency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSecond-generation Outposts racks support the latest generation of x86-powered Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances, starting with general purpose M7i instances, compute-optimized C7i instances, and memory-optimized R7i instances. These instances deliver twice the virtual CPU, memory, and network bandwidth, and up to 40% better performance compared to C5, M5, and R5 instances on first-generation Outposts racks. Second-generation Outposts racks also feature a new networking architecture that has built-in resiliency to handle network device failures and enables decoupling of compute and networking and self-service local gateway (LGW) configurations. These advancements simplify network operations and enable cost-efficient scaling of on-premises workloads. The launch also introduces a new category of EC2 instances for AWS Outposts racks with accelerated networking. These instances feature specialized network accelerator cards and are designed for the most latency-sensitive, compute-intensive, and throughput-intensive on-premises workloads such as core trading systems of financial exchanges, real-time market data distribution, telecom 5G core, and media distribution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWith second-generation Outposts racks, you can continue to leverage the same APIs, management console, automation, governance policies, and security controls for your applications across AWS Regions and on-premises locations. This allows you to centralize infrastructure management and boost developer productivity by standardizing on a common set of continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipelines.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor a current list of AWS Regions and countries/territories where Outposts racks are supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-is-outposts-rack-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, read this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/announcing-second-generation-aws-outposts-racks-with-breakthrough-performance-and-scalability-on-premises/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/04/second-generation-aws-outposts-racks","postDateTime":"2025-04-29T16:10:00-04:00","headline":"Announcing second-generation AWS Outposts racks"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1703806728","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"54RHCrEWhPCf3PPoy1azPY","dateCreated":"2025-03-21T16:05:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-03-31T17:01:17+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/03/asset-level-capacity-management-aws-outposts","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts now supports self-service capacity management that can be defined specifically for each individual asset. An Outpost asset can be a single server within an Outposts rack or an Outposts server. This makes it easy for customers to customize the allocation of capacity on Outposts at a more granular level. Outposts brings native AWS services, AWS infrastructure, and operating models to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility by providing the same services, tools, and partner solutions with Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) on premises. Customers have evolving business requirements and often need to fine-tune their application needs as their businesses scale. Capacity management, now with asset level control, enables viewing and modifying the configuration of EC2 capacity on any Outposts.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nCustomers can define the configuration of EC2 instances on each Outposts rack or server when they place an Outposts order. Customers can then utilize capacity management to view these EC2 instances on their Outposts, their configured sizes, and their placement within the Outpost. Customers can also use capacity management to view, plan, and modify their capacity configuration through self-service UI and API.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nCapacity management is available in all AWS Regions where Outposts are supported. Check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e for the list of supported Regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about these new capacity management capabilities for Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-capacity.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts user guide\u003c/a\u003e. To discuss Outposts for your on-premises workloads with an Outposts specialist, submit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/GLOBAL_PM_LN_outposts-features_2020084_7010z000001Lpcl_01.LandingPage.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis form\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2025-03-31T13:00:00-04:00","headline":"Asset level capacity management for AWS Outposts"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p199353409","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-qoDXTC2nNPc2z3aFHybey3","dateCreated":"2025-02-28T19:29:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-03-03T18:17:45+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/03/aws-outposts-racks-throughput-network-intensive-workloads/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS announces the preview of new AWS Outposts racks designed specifically for on-premises high throughput, network-intensive workloads. With these new Outposts racks, telecom service providers (telcos) can extend AWS infrastructure and services to telco locations, enabling them to deploy on-premises network functions requiring low latency, high throughput, and real-time performance.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe new Outposts racks feature new Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) 4th Generation Intel Xeon Scalable-based (Sapphire Rapids) bare metal instances along with a high-performance bare metal network fabric. This architecture delivers the low latency and high throughput required for demanding 5G workloads, such as User Plane Function (UPF) and Radio Access Network (RAN) Central Unit (CU) network functions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTelcos can now use Amazon EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service) and built-in EKS add-ons to automate deployment and scaling of micro-services based 5G network functions for high throughput and performance. Telcos can now use the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, tools, and a common continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipeline wherever their workloads reside. This consistent cloud experience eases operational burden, reduces integration costs, and maximizes new feature development velocity for operators.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe new AWS Outposts racks are currently available in preview in the following AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Europe (Frankfurt), and Asia Pacific (Singapore).\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2025-03-03T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"Announcing AWS Outposts racks for high throughput, network-intensive workloads (Preview)"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launchmarketingintake-1428","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"oVJWFsdkUAQeLCAzD41b9w","dateCreated":"2024-11-25T21:54:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-01T21:56:41+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can attach block data volumes backed by NetApp\u0026reg; on-premises enterprise storage arrays and Pure Storage\u0026reg; FlashArray\u0026trade; to Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances on AWS Outposts directly from the AWS Management Console. This makes it easier for customers to leverage third-party storage with Outposts. Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith this enhancement, Outpost customers can combine the cloud capabilities offered by Outposts with advanced data management features, high density storage, and high performance offered by NetApp on-premises enterprise storage arrays and Pure Storage FlashArray. Today, customers can use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) and Local Instance Store volumes to store and process data locally and comply with data residency requirements. Now, with this enhancement, they can do so while leveraging the external volumes backed by compatible third-party storage. By leveraging the new enhancement, customers can maximize value from their existing storage investments, while benefiting from the cloud operational model enabled by Outposts.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis enhancement is available on Outposts racks and Outposts 2U servers at no additional charge in all AWS Regions where Outposts is available, except the AWS GovCloud Regions. See the FAQs for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts racks\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\"\u003e \u003c/a\u003efor the latest availability information.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nYou can use the AWS Management Console or CLI to attach the third-party block data volumes to Amazon EC2 instances on Outposts. To learn more, check out this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/new-simplifying-the-use-of-third-party-block-storage-with-aws-outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/12/aws-third-party-block-storage-arrays-outposts","postDateTime":"2024-12-01T13:00:00-05:00","headline":"AWS simplifies the use of third-party block storage arrays with AWS Outposts"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p170212201","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-fgoPi67cDLYbuuKmZTRSLm","dateCreated":"2024-11-21T00:32:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-25T17:28:28+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts now offers static stability for Amazon EC2 instances backed by EC2 instance store. This enables automatic recovery for workloads running on such EC2 instances from power failures or reboots, even when the connection to the parent AWS Region is temporarily unavailable. This means Outposts servers and Outposts racks can recover faster from power outages, minimizing downtime and data loss.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nOutposts provides a consistent hybrid experience by bringing AWS services to customer premises and edge locations on fully managed AWS infrastructure. While Outposts typically runs connected to an AWS Region for resource management, access control, and software updates, the new static stability feature enables workloads running on EC2 instances backed by EC2 instance store to recover from power failures even when connectivity to the AWS Region is unavailable. Note that this capability is currently not available for EC2 instances backed by Amazon EBS volumes.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis capability is in all AWS Regions where Outposts is supported. Check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e for the full list of supported Regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo get started, no customer specific action is required. Static stability is now enabled for all EC2 instances backed by EC2 instance store.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/static-stability-amazon-ec2-instances-store-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2024-11-22T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"Announcing static stability for Amazon EC2 instances backed by EC2 instance store on AWS Outposts"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p165587034","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-1yQr7TtxdNLCB27z3A14rR","dateCreated":"2024-11-11T19:07:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-18T18:13:49+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/self-service-capacity-management-aws-outposts/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts now supports self-service capacity management making it easy for you to view and manage compute capacity on your Outposts. Outposts brings native AWS services, infrastructure, and operating models to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility by providing the same services, tools, and partner solutions with EC2 on premises. Customers have evolving business requirements and often need to fine-tune their application needs as their business scales. Capacity management enables viewing and modifying the configuration of EC2 capacity installed on Outposts.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nCustomers define their configuration when ordering a new Outposts to support a variety of different instances. Customers utilize capacity management to view these instances on their Outposts, their configured sizes, and their placement within the Outposts. Customers can also use capacity management to view, plan, and modify their capacity configuration which they will customize through this new self-service UI and API.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThese capacity management features are available in all AWS Regions where Outposts is supported. Check out the Outposts rack FAQs page and the Outposts servers FAQs page for the full list of supported Regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about these capacity management capabilities for Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-capacity.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts user guide\u003c/a\u003e. To discuss Outposts capacity needs for your on-premises workloads with an Outposts specialist, submit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/GLOBAL_PM_LN_outposts-features_2020084_7010z000001Lpcl_01.LandingPage.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis form\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2024-11-18T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"Self-service capacity management for AWS Outposts"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p158714159","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"kCC51T4UxiGMdq9GnczE4r","dateCreated":"2024-10-03T19:10:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-10-07T17:06:36+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region. Outposts is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nOrganizations from startups to enterprises and the public sector in and outside of Spain can now connect their Outposts to this Region. Outposts allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers\u0026rsquo; Outposts can connect to.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/10/aws-outposts-europe-spain-region","postDateTime":"2024-10-07T13:00:00-04:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts supported in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p154043546","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-aLZ5T5xXf4WCzJfgTBLJ5F","dateCreated":"2024-09-24T16:50:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-27T17:44:40+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/09/aws-outposts-kuwait/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Kuwait.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Outposts is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith the availability of Outposts in Kuwait, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-is-outposts-rack-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-are-outposts-servers-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2024-09-27T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Kuwait"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p142754327","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"5Zg5UtdoCdFmp6AwNYEmA9","dateCreated":"2024-07-23T19:11:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-20T16:59:14+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Jordan.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Outposts is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith the availability of Outposts in Jordan, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-is-outposts-rack-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-are-outposts-servers-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/09/availability-aws-outposts-jordan","postDateTime":"2024-09-20T13:00:00-04:00","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Jordan"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p124959142","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"6EQ29pKSfkSSj8iysbEws9","dateCreated":"2024-07-02T17:19:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-11T17:03:48+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Senegal.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Outposts is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith the availability of Outposts in Senegal, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-is-outposts-rack-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/#product-faqs%23in-which-countries-and-territories-are-outposts-servers-available-trigger\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/07/availability-aws-outposts-senegal","postDateTime":"2024-07-11T13:00:00-04:00","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Senegal"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-04-aws-elastic-disaster-recovery-outposts-racks","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/04/aws-elastic-disaster-recovery-outposts-racks/","dateCreated":"2024-04-19T17:10:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:00:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/disaster-recovery/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Elastic Disaster Recovery\u003c/a\u003e (AWS DRS) announces support of AWS Outposts racks. With this launch, you can now set your data replication and recovery destinations to AWS Outposts racks, in addition to using AWS Regions and Availability Zones where AWS DRS is available. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS DRS minimizes downtime and data loss with fast, reliable recovery of on-premises and cloud-based applications using affordable storage, minimal compute, and point-in-time recovery. With AWS Outposts, a family of fully managed solutions delivering AWS infrastructure and services to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience, you can run some AWS services locally and connect to a broad range of services available in the local AWS Region. With this change, you can get the same functionality of AWS DRS while creating the AWS resources required to operate the replication or recovery inside your AWS Outposts racks, keeping these resources within your premises.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new capability is available in all AWS Regions where AWS DRS is available. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regional Services List\u003c/a\u003e for the latest availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about AWS DRS, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/disaster-recovery/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/drs/latest/userguide/what-is-drs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, sign in to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.amazonaws-us-gov.com/drs/home?region\u003dus-gov-west-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Elastic Disaster Recovery Console\u003c/a\u003e.  To learn more about AWS Outposts, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts racks product page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-04-19T17:10:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/04/aws-elastic-disaster-recovery-outposts-racks/","postDateTime":"2024-04-19T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery now supports AWS Outposts Racks","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/disaster-recovery.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Elastic Disaster Recovery\u003c/a\u003e (AWS DRS) announces support of AWS Outposts racks. With this launch, you can now set your data replication and recovery destinations to AWS Outposts racks, in addition to using AWS Regions and Availability Zones where AWS DRS is available. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-elastic-disaster-recovery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-elastic-disaster-recovery","description":"general:products/aws-elastic-disaster-recovery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:37:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-04-availability-aws-outposts-kingdom-saudi-arabia","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/04/availability-aws-outposts-kingdom-saudi-arabia/","dateCreated":"2024-04-08T20:34:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:59:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAs of this date, customers deploying in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia may require additional authorization. Contact your AWS Sales Representative to learn more. To get started or learn more about Outposts,\u0026nbsp;read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-04-08T20:52:07Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/04/availability-aws-outposts-kingdom-saudi-arabia/","postDateTime":"2024-04-08T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-03-amazon-s3-outposts-first-byte-latencies-object-api-requests","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/03/amazon-s3-outposts-first-byte-latencies-object-api-requests/","dateCreated":"2024-03-13T17:10:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now caches AWS IAM permissions locally, improving the performance of applications running on AWS Outposts. This local cache eliminates the variability in first-byte latencies that comes from authentication and authorization operations in the parent AWS Region, which improves the performance of your object API requests.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAfter you make an API request to S3 on Outposts, AWS IAM permissions for S3 on Outposts are securely cached locally on the Outpost. Your subsequent S3 object API requests will be authenticated and authorized using cached data, eliminating the latency incurred from a round trip to the AWS Region. The cache will be valid for up to 10 minutes when the Outpost is connected to the AWS Region, and will be refreshed asynchronously when you make an S3 on Outposts API request, so that the latest permissions are used. To take advantage of the local cache, you need to sign API requests with the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_aws-signing.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eSigV4A\u003c/a\u003e algorithm, which is available in the latest versions of the AWS SDKs, and is obtained through a dependency on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdkref/latest/guide/common-runtime.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Common Runtime (CRT)\u003c/a\u003e libraries.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e Support for S3 on Outposts authentication and authorization cache is available in all AWS Regions where S3 on Outposts is available at no additional cost. To get started or learn more, visit\u0026nbsp;the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-03-13T17:10:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/03/amazon-s3-outposts-first-byte-latencies-object-api-requests/","postDateTime":"2024-03-13T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts reduces first-byte latencies for object API requests","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now caches AWS IAM permissions locally, improving the performance of applications running on AWS Outposts. This local cache eliminates the variability in first-byte latencies that comes from authentication and authorization operations in the parent AWS Region, which improves the performance of your object API requests.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-01-aws-outposts-turkey","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/aws-outposts-turkey/","dateCreated":"2024-02-02T13:31:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:05:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Turkey.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in Turkey, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-01-09T18:01:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/aws-outposts-turkey/","postDateTime":"2024-01-09T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Turkey","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Turkey.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-aws-outposts-rack-service-link-interface-throughput-metrics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/aws-outposts-rack-service-link-interface-throughput-metrics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-20T18:05:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:54:18+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now monitor network throughput between your Outpost rack service link virtual interfaces (VIFs) and your local network devices using Amazon CloudWatch IfTrafficIn and IfTrafficOut metrics for Outposts. Outpost rack service link VIFs establish IP connectivity and BGP sessions between your Outpost and your local network devices for service link connectivity.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith this enhancement, you can now monitor the volume of data transferred (in bits per second) between your Outpost rack service link VIFs and your local network devices in inbound and outbound directions by using CloudWatch. These metrics give visibility into network usage and help with troubleshooting local network issues. Additionally, by combining these metrics with the existing local gateway VIFs throughput metrics, you and your networking team can gain a complete view of the bandwidth requirements for your local network infrastructure to support traffic to and from your Outposts. You can access both service link and local gateway VIFs IfTrafficIn and IfTrafficOut metrics in CloudWatch.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eService link VIFs throughput CloudWatch metrics are available in all AWS Regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ewhere Outposts rack is available\u003c/a\u003e, except the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-cloudwatch-metrics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloudWatch metrics for AWS Outposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-20T18:04:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/aws-outposts-rack-service-link-interface-throughput-metrics/","postDateTime":"2023-11-20T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts rack supports service link interface throughput metrics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now monitor network throughput between your Outpost rack service link virtual interfaces (VIFs) and your local network devices using Amazon CloudWatch IfTrafficIn and IfTrafficOut metrics for Outposts. Outpost rack service link VIFs establish IP connectivity and BGP sessions between your Outpost and your local network devices for service link connectivity.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-aws-outposts-rack-intra-vpc-communication-multiple-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-outposts-rack-intra-vpc-communication-multiple-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now add routes in your AWS Outposts rack subnet route table to forward traffic between subnets within the same VPC spanning across disparate Outposts, using the Outpost local gateways (LGW). The LGW enables connectivity between your Outpost subnets and your on-premises network. With this enhancement, you can establish intra-VPC instance-to-instance IP communication across Outposts through your on-premise network, via direct VPC routing (DVR).\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eUntil today, in order to establish communication between instances across Outposts, you needed to create subnets in different VPCs or use separate IP address range/CIDR, known as a CoIP pool. With this launch, you can leverage single VPC architecture for communications between instances across Outposts and utilize DVR, removing complexity of managing separate VPC and CoIP pools. You can use this feature to build multi-AZ like architectures for your on-premise applications running on Outposts racks that are anchored to two different AZs.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIntra-VPC communication across multiple Outposts is available in all AWS Regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ewhere Outposts rack is available\u003c/a\u003e. Your existing Outposts racks may require an update to enable support for intra-VPC communication across multiple Outposts. If this feature does not work for you, please contact \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/case-management.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, check out this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/introducing-intra-vpc-communication-across-multiple-outposts-with-direct-vpc-routing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/features/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack feature page\u003c/a\u003e, and the Outposts \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/how-outposts-works.html#routing-hiw\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-30T20:39:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-outposts-rack-intra-vpc-communication-multiple-outposts/","postDateTime":"2023-08-30T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts rack now supports intra-VPC communication across multiple Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now add routes in your AWS Outposts rack subnet route table to forward traffic between subnets within the same VPC spanning across disparate Outposts, using the Outpost local gateways (LGW). The LGW enables connectivity between your Outpost subnets and your on-premises network. With this enhancement, you can establish intra-VPC instance-to-instance IP communication across Outposts through your on-premise network, via direct VPC routing (DVR).\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-aws-outposts-iceland-uruguay","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-outposts-iceland-uruguay/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:04:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your datacenter and on-premises locations in Iceland and Uruguay.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in Iceland and Uruguay, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-29T21:35:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-outposts-iceland-uruguay/","postDateTime":"2023-08-29T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Iceland and Uruguay","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your datacenter and on-premises locations in Iceland and Uruguay.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-aws-outposts-rack-middle-east-uae-israel-tel-aviv-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-outposts-rack-middle-east-uae-israel-tel-aviv-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:03:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack is now supported in the AWS Middle East (UAE) and the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Regions. AWS Outposts rack is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eOrganizations from startups to enterprise and the public sector in and outside of UAE and Israel can now connect their Outposts to these regions. AWS Outposts rack allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to their home region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts rack and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on-premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-22T17:13:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-outposts-rack-middle-east-uae-israel-tel-aviv-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-08-22T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts rack supported in the AWS Middle East (UAE) and the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack is now supported in the AWS Middle East (UAE) and the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Regions. AWS Outposts rack is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-07-amazon-route-53-resolver-aws-outposts-rack","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/07/amazon-route-53-resolver-aws-outposts-rack/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:00:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can enable Amazon Route 53 Resolver on AWS Outpost rack, allowing you to resolve Domain Name Server (DNS) queries locally and enhance the availability and performance of applications running on Outposts rack.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eOutposts rack is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure and AWS services on premises for a truly consistent hybrid experience. When you enable Route 53 Resolver on Outposts, Route 53 automatically stores DNS responses locally on your Outposts. Optionally, you can connect Route 53 Resolvers on your Outposts with DNS servers in your on-premises data centers using Route 53 Resolver endpoints. Route 53 Resolver on Outposts provides continued DNS resolution during unexpected network disconnects to the parent Region. By serving DNS responses locally, Route 53 Resolver on Outposts also improves the performance of your on-premises applications.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, enable Route 53 Resolver at the time of ordering a new Outpost. You can also work with your AWS team to add Route 53 Resolver to an existing Outpost. You can create and manage the Route 53 Resolver on Outposts using Route 53 APIs, the AWS Management Console, the AWS CLI, or the AWS SDKs.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eRoute 53 Resolver on Outposts is available in all AWS Regions where Outposts rack is available, except in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs\u003c/a\u003e for the full list of Regions where Outposts is available. To learn more, check out \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-route-53-resolver-now-available-on-aws-outposts-rack\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ethis blog post\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack pricing page\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/outpost-resolver.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eRoute 53 Resolver documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-07-21T17:37:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/07/amazon-route-53-resolver-aws-outposts-rack/","postDateTime":"2023-07-21T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Route 53 Resolver now available on AWS Outposts rack","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can enable Amazon Route 53 Resolver on AWS Outpost rack, allowing you to resolve Domain Name Server (DNS) queries locally and enhance the availability and performance of applications running on Outposts rack.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-route-53","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-route-53","description":"general:products/amazon-route-53","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-ec2-dedicated-hosts-allocations-outposts-rack","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-ec2-dedicated-hosts-allocations-outposts-rack/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:59:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:49:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now target allocation of Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts to specific AWS Outpost hosts. With targeted Dedicated Host allocations, you can control the deployment location of your workloads on specific Outposts racks. This allows you to allocate Dedicated Hosts on physical servers closely located on the same Outposts rack to achieve low latency goals. You can also use this feature to spread workloads on hardware across multiple Outposts racks for additional resiliency.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eDedicated Hosts on Outposts now allows you to specify the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/APIReference/API_AssetInfo.html#outposts-Type-AssetInfo-AssetId\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAssetID\u003c/a\u003e associated\u0026nbsp;with a physical server in your Outposts rack when allocating a new Dedicated Host using the EC2 Console, AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), or an Amazon CloudFormation template. You may specify multiple target \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/APIReference/API_AssetInfo.html#outposts-Type-AssetInfo-AssetId\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAssetID’s\u003c/a\u003e for\u0026nbsp;allocating more than one host. You can also view the Asset ID associated with an allocated Dedicated Host in Outposts using EC2 Console or the EC2 \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/ec2/describe-hosts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edescribe-hosts API\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEC2 Dedicated Hosts on Outposts simplify bringing your existing software licenses and workloads requiring a dedicated physical server to the cloud. You can benefit from the flexibility and cost efficiency of using your eligible software licenses that are bound to VMs, sockets, or physical cores on Dedicated Hosts. In addition, with Dedicated Hosts you can exercise granular EC2 instance placement control based on your business needs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available for Dedicated Hosts on AWS Outposts connected to all AWS Commercial Regions. It is not yet available in AWS GovCloud and China regions.\u0026nbsp;To learn more,\u0026nbsp;visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/dh-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDedicated Hosts on AWS Outposts User Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003csup\u003e6/23/2023 -\u0026nbsp;Targeted allocation of Dedicated Hosts on AWS Outposts rack is not yet available in AWS GovCloud and China regions.\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-06-23T17:43:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-ec2-dedicated-hosts-allocations-outposts-rack/","postDateTime":"2023-06-23T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts now support targeted allocations in AWS Outposts rack","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now target allocation of Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts to specific AWS Outpost hosts. With targeted Dedicated Host allocations, you can control the deployment location of your workloads on specific Outposts racks. This allows you to allocate Dedicated Hosts on physical servers closely located on the same Outposts rack to achieve low latency goals. You can also use this feature to spread workloads on hardware across multiple Outposts racks for additional resiliency.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-s3-outposts-local-s3-replication-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-s3-outposts-local-s3-replication-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:58:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports S3 Replication on Outposts. This extends S3’s fully managed approach to replication to S3 on Outposts buckets, helping you meet data residency and data redundancy requirements. With local S3 Replication on Outposts, you can create and configure replication rules to automatically replicate your S3 objects to another Outpost, or to another bucket on the same Outpost. During replication, your S3 on Outposts objects are always sent over your local gateway (LGW), and objects do not travel back to the AWS Region. S3 Replication on Outposts provides an easy and flexible way to automatically replicate data within a specific data perimeter to address your data redundancy and compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith S3 Replication on Outposts, you can replicate objects to a single Outpost destination bucket or to multiple destination buckets. The destination buckets can be in different AWS Outposts or within the same Outpost as the source bucket. As with S3 Replication in regions today, you can select to replicate all the items in your bucket, or you can filter to select objects based on prefix, object tags, or a combination of both. S3 Replication on Outposts also provides detailed metrics and notifications to monitor the status of your object replication. You can monitor replication progress by tracking bytes pending, operations pending, and replication latency between your source and destination Outposts buckets using Amazon CloudWatch. You can also set up EventBridge Notifications to receive replication failure notifications to quickly diagnose and correct configuration issues.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for S3 Replication on Outposts is now available at no additional cost in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions where AWS Outposts racks are available\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with replication visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3-outposts/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e, or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/S3OutpostsReplication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-03-14T18:00:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-s3-outposts-local-s3-replication-outposts/","postDateTime":"2023-03-14T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts now supports local S3 Replication on Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports S3 Replication on Outposts. This extends S3’s fully managed approach to replication to S3 on Outposts buckets, helping you meet data residency and data redundancy requirements. With local S3 Replication on Outposts, you can create and configure replication rules to automatically replicate your S3 objects to another Outpost, or to another bucket on the same Outpost. During replication, your S3 on Outposts objects are always sent over your local gateway (LGW), and objects do not travel back to the AWS Region. S3 Replication on Outposts provides an easy and flexible way to automatically replicate data within a specific data perimeter to address your data redundancy and compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-01-aws-outposts-rack-local-gateway-vpc-prefix-lists-routing-policy-manager","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/01/aws-outposts-rack-local-gateway-vpc-prefix-lists-routing-policy-manager/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:59:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:51:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack local gateway now supports Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) prefix lists, simplifying management of your routing policies to connect to your on-premises network.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack, a part of the AWS Outposts family, is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Each Outpost provides a local gateway that allows you to connect your Outpost resources with your on-premises networks. Prefix lists allow you to group one or more CIDR blocks into a single object. You can group CIDRs that you frequently use in a prefix list, and reference this list as a route target in your local gateway route table. Previously, you needed to add individual routes when scaling your network to add a new CIDR block, which could be time-consuming and error-prone. Now you can update the relevant prefix list by adding or removing CIDR blocks and all routes in the local gateway route table referencing the prefix list are automatically updated. As you scale your network, prefix lists can help simplify management of your local gateway on your Outpost.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC prefix lists for Outposts rack local gateway are available via the Amazon VPC Console or the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-local-gateways.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutpost local gateway API\u003c/a\u003e in all AWS Regions where AWS Outposts rack is available. There is no additional charge for using prefix lists with AWS Outposts rack. To get started with AWS Outposts rack, please see the AWS Outposts rack \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and service \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-01-30T22:25:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/01/aws-outposts-rack-local-gateway-vpc-prefix-lists-routing-policy-manager/","postDateTime":"2023-01-30T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts rack local gateway now supports VPC prefix lists to simplify routing policy management","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack local gateway now supports Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) prefix lists, simplifying management of your routing policies to connect to your on-premises network.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-rds-aws-outposts-supports-read-replicas-mysql-postgresql","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-rds-aws-outposts-supports-read-replicas-mysql-postgresql/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:57:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:48:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on AWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports Read Replicas. Amazon RDS Read Replicas provide enhanced performance and durability for RDS database (DB) instances. They provide the option to elastically scale out beyond the capacity constraints of a single DB instance for read-heavy database workloads. You can create one or more replicas of a given source DB instance and serve high-volume application read traffic from multiple copies of your data, thereby increasing aggregate read throughput. Read replicas can also be promoted when needed to become standalone DB instances.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS on AWS Outposts now also allows you to create \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/features/read-replicas/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eRead Replicas\u003c/a\u003e of your DB instances on the same Outpost or across Outposts, providing both scale out read performance as well as part of a disaster recovery solution. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, you may also create Amazon RDS Read Replicas on Amazon RDS Multi-AZ instance deployments on Outposts, which can provide additional disaster recovery capabilities to your highly-available Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts instances.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-on-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS on AWS Outposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e. Get started creating Amazon RDS Read Replica DB instances on Outposts on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/rds/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-19T20:48:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-rds-aws-outposts-supports-read-replicas-mysql-postgresql/","postDateTime":"2022-12-19T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts now supports read replicas for MySQL and PostgreSQL","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/rds/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on AWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports Read Replicas. Amazon RDS Read Replicas provide enhanced performance and durability for RDS database (DB) instances. They provide the option to elastically scale out beyond the capacity constraints of a single DB instance for read-heavy database workloads. You can create one or more replicas of a given source DB instance and serve high-volume application read traffic from multiple copies of your data, thereby increasing aggregate read throughput. Read replicas can also be promoted when needed to become standalone DB instances.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-aws-outposts-egypt","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/aws-outposts-egypt/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:28:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Egypt.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in Egypt, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-07T23:02:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/aws-outposts-egypt/","postDateTime":"2022-12-07T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Egypt","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Egypt.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-outposts-qatar-guatemala-trinidad-tobago","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-outposts-qatar-guatemala-trinidad-tobago/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Qatar, Guatemala, and Trinidad \u0026amp; Tobago.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a family of fully managed solutions that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts can also help meet data residency requirements. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks, and multiple rack deployments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in Qatar, Guatemala, and Trinidad \u0026amp; Tobago, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations. Outposts rack is now available in 73 countries and territories, and 2U Outposts servers are now available in 72 countries and territories.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and\u0026nbsp;the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-30T00:19:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-outposts-qatar-guatemala-trinidad-tobago/","postDateTime":"2022-11-29T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Qatar, Guatemala, and Trinidad \u0026 Tobago","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Qatar, Guatemala, and Trinidad \u0026amp; Tobago.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-outposts-rack-service-bangladesh","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-outposts-rack-service-bangladesh/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:01:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Bangladesh.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack, a part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts family\u003c/a\u003e, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts rack is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts rack can also help meet data residency requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts rack in Bangladesh, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts rack, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of AWS Regions where Outposts rack is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-02T19:36:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-outposts-rack-service-bangladesh/","postDateTime":"2022-11-02T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts rack service in Bangladesh","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Bangladesh.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-s3-outposts-optimizes-storage-management-new-lifecycle-actions-filters","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-s3-outposts-optimizes-storage-management-new-lifecycle-actions-filters/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:40:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports additional S3 Lifecycle rules to optimize capacity management. You can now optimize your storage capacity by expiring objects as they age or are replaced with newer versions. You can use S3 Lifecycle configurations for a whole bucket on your Outpost, or for a subset of the objects in the bucket by filtering by prefixes, object tags, or object sizes.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePrior to this release, you could use Lifecycle rules to initiate object deletion based on age or date. Now, you have additional fine-grained controls to expire current versions of objects and permanently delete non-current versions of objects. This allows you to more easily optimize your S3 on Outposts storage capacity.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts rack environment to help you meet your low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. Outposts rack, as part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts Family\u003c/a\u003e, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eLifecycle rules are available at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts rack is available\u003c/a\u003e. To get started or learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e, or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-02T17:11:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-s3-outposts-optimizes-storage-management-new-lifecycle-actions-filters/","postDateTime":"2022-11-02T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts further optimizes storage management with new Lifecycle actions and filters","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports additional S3 Lifecycle rules to optimize capacity management. You can now optimize your storage capacity by expiring objects as they age or are replaced with newer versions. You can use S3 Lifecycle configurations for a whole bucket on your Outpost, or for a subset of the objects in the bucket by filtering by prefixes, object tags, or object sizes.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-amazon-s3-outposts-supports-object-versioning","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-s3-outposts-supports-object-versioning/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:41:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports versioning, helping you to locally preserve, retrieve, and restore each version of every object stored in your buckets. Versioning objects makes it easier to recover from both unintended user actions and application failures.  After you enable versioning for your S3 on Outposts bucket, all variants of an object are stored in the same bucket, and are distinguishable by a versionId. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts rack environment to help you meet your low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. AWS Outposts rack, as part of the AWS Outposts Family, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for S3 versioning is available to S3 on Outposts customers at no additional charge, in all AWS Regions where Outposts rack is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eavailable\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e, or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-21T17:03:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-s3-outposts-supports-object-versioning/","postDateTime":"2022-09-21T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts now supports object versioning","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports versioning, helping you to locally preserve, retrieve, and restore each version of every object stored in your buckets. Versioning objects makes it easier to recover from both unintended user actions and application failures.  After you enable versioning for your S3 on Outposts bucket, all variants of an object are stored in the same bucket, and are distinguishable by a versionId. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-aws-outposts-rack-kazakhstan-serbia","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/aws-outposts-rack-kazakhstan-serbia/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:28:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Kazakhstan and Serbia.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack, a part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts family\u003c/a\u003e, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts rack is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts rack can also help meet data residency requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts rack in Kazakhstan and Serbia you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts rack, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of AWS Regions where Outposts rack is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-21T18:57:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/aws-outposts-rack-kazakhstan-serbia/","postDateTime":"2022-09-21T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts rack in Kazakhstan and Serbia","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Kazakhstan and Serbia.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-amazon-eks-outposts-local-clusters","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-eks-outposts-local-clusters/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:37:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are excited to announce the general availability of local clusters for Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) on Outposts, which enable you to run highly available Kubernetes clusters in on-premises environments. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eLocal clusters enable you to run the entire Amazon EKS cluster locally on Outposts, so you can mitigate the risk of application downtime that can result from temporary network disconnects to the cloud, such as those caused by fiber cuts or weather events. Because the entire Kubernetes cluster runs locally on Outposts, applications remain available, and you can perform cluster operations during network disconnects to the cloud. When connected to the cloud, Amazon EKS manages the availability of the Kubernetes control plane on Outposts, so you can simplify your Kubernetes operations. Local clusters run the same Kubernetes as Amazon EKS in the cloud, and automatically deploy the latest security patches to make it easier for you to maintain an up-to-date, secure cluster. You can use the same tooling you use with Amazon EKS in the cloud for a consistent experience across on-premises and cloud environments.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eLocal clusters are generally available for use with Outposts racks. You can create local clusters from the following AWS Regions: US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), US West (N. California), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (London), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), South America (São Paulo), Middle East (Bahrain).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eGet started by creating a cluster via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/eks/home#/clusters\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EKS console\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/contact-us/sales-support-eks/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econnect with an Amazon EKS on Outposts specialist\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/deploy-your-amazon-eks-clusters-locally-on-aws-outposts\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e or visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-outposts-local-cluster-overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-20T16:40:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-eks-outposts-local-clusters/","postDateTime":"2022-09-20T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing local clusters for Amazon EKS on Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are excited to announce the general availability of local clusters for Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) on Outposts, which enable you to run highly available Kubernetes clusters in on-premises environments. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T18:48:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-local-gateway-ingress-routing-aws-outposts-rack-now-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/local-gateway-ingress-routing-aws-outposts-rack-now-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:49:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now create Outposts rack local gateway (LGW) inbound routes\u0026nbsp;to redirect incoming traffic to an elastic network interface (ENI) attached to an Amazon EC2 instance before the traffic reaches your enterprise workloads running on your Outpost. The EC2 instance may run virtual network appliance software to inspect, modify, or filter network traffic before relaying the traffic to other EC2 instances.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack installed at customer locations uses LGW for communication between your Outpost and on-premises traffic. With AWS Outposts rack LGW ingress routing, you can now create an ENI for your virtual network appliance to receive traffic from the local network destined for any IP address range that do not belong to VPCs on Outposts rack. This enables you to use LGW ingress routing to steer traffic to an EC2 instance on the Outposts rack functioning as a virtual network appliance, thereby creating the fine-grained network and security policies for your workload.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts rack local gateway ingress routing, read this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/deploying-local-gateway-ingress-routing-on-aws-outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e. To find out more about Outposts rack, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts website\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/console/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-15T21:31:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/local-gateway-ingress-routing-aws-outposts-rack-now-available/","postDateTime":"2022-09-15T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Local gateway ingress routing for AWS Outposts rack is now available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now create Outposts rack local gateway (LGW) inbound routes\u0026nbsp;to redirect incoming traffic to an elastic network interface (ENI) attached to an Amazon EC2 instance before the traffic reaches your enterprise workloads running on your Outpost. The EC2 instance may run virtual network appliance software to inspect, modify, or filter network traffic before relaying the traffic to other EC2 instances.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-direct-vpc-routing-aws-outposts-rack","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/direct-vpc-routing-aws-outposts-rack/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:49:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWith direct VPC routing for AWS Outposts rack, you can now directly use the VPC private IP address of an Amazon EC2 instance on Outposts rack to communicate with your on-premises network. This new direct VPC routing mode is an alternative to the Customer-owned IP (CoIP) routing mode where Outposts rack uses a separate IP address pool provided by you from your on-premises network.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eUntil today, during an Outposts rack installation, you had to provide a separate IP address range/CIDR from your on-premises network for AWS to create an address pool, known as a CoIP pool. When an EC2 instance on your Outposts rack needed to communicate with your on-premises network, Outposts rack would perform a 1:1 network address translation (NAT) from the VPC private IP address to a CoIP address in the CoIP pool. Outposts rack now supports a new direct VPC routing mode where you can simply use the VPC private IP of the EC2 instance for routing traffic between your Outpost and your on-premises network. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eDirect VPC routing is available in all AWS Regions where Outposts rack is supported. You can choose CoIP or direct VPC routing mode depending on your local network needs. Outposts rack will continue to support CoIP mode for those who prefer to use separate on-premises IP ranges for routing in on-premises networks.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts racks website\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/routing.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e for more details. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-14T22:00:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/direct-vpc-routing-aws-outposts-rack/","postDateTime":"2022-09-14T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Direct VPC routing for AWS Outposts rack is now available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWith direct VPC routing for AWS Outposts rack, you can now directly use the VPC private IP address of an Amazon EC2 instance on Outposts rack to communicate with your on-premises network. This new direct VPC routing mode is an alternative to the Customer-owned IP (CoIP) routing mode where Outposts rack uses a separate IP address pool provided by you from your on-premises network.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-enterprise-on-ramp-supported-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/enterprise-on-ramp-supported-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:59:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers now have the option of using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/premiumsupport/plans/enterprise-onramp/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEnterprise On-Ramp Support\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/premiumsupport/plans/enterprise/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEnterprise Support\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to satisfy the prerequisite for ordering \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. With the addition of Enterprise On-Ramp Support, customers now have more flexibility in selecting the AWS Support plan that best suits their Outposts workloads and support needs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a family of fully managed solutions delivering AWS infrastructure and services to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Launched in re:Invent 2021, Enterprise On-Ramp Support is a new AWS Support tier between the existing Business Support tier and Enterprise Support tier to help customers that are starting their cloud journey and need expert guidance to grow and optimize on cloud. Enterprise On-Ramp Support includes 24/7 access to Support engineers with 30 minute case response time for high severity issues. Customers also get access to consultative architectural guidance, operations reviews, cost optimization recommendations, and event management support delivered by a pool of Technical Account Managers (TAMs).\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Enterprise Support and Enterprise On-Ramp Support to determine which plan is better suited to your use case, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/premiumsupport/plans/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCompare AWS Support Plans\u003c/a\u003e. To find out more about AWS Outposts, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-01T18:58:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/enterprise-on-ramp-supported-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2022-09-01T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Enterprise On-Ramp Support is now supported with AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers now have the option of using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/premiumsupport/plans/enterprise-onramp.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEnterprise On-Ramp Support\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/premiumsupport/plans/enterprise.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEnterprise Support\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to satisfy the prerequisite for ordering \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. With the addition of Enterprise On-Ramp Support, customers now have more flexibility in selecting the AWS Support plan that best suits their Outposts workloads and support needs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-08-aws-outposts-rack-kenya-oman","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/08/aws-outposts-rack-kenya-oman/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:15:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Kenya and Oman.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack, a part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts family\u003c/a\u003e, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts rack is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies. Outposts rack can also help meet data residency requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts rack in Kenya and Oman, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts rack, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of AWS Regions where Outposts rack is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-08-25T19:03:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/08/aws-outposts-rack-kenya-oman/","postDateTime":"2022-08-25T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts rack in Kenya and Oman","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Kenya and Oman.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-07-aws-outposts-rack-supported-aws-asia-pacific-jakarta-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/07/aws-outposts-rack-supported-aws-asia-pacific-jakarta-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:43:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack is now supported in AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region. AWS Outposts rack is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eOrganizations from startups to enterprise and the public sector in and outside of Indonesia can now connect their Outposts to the AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region. AWS Outposts rack allows customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to the AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region for application management. Customers can also use Outposts rack and AWS services to manage and process data that needs to remain on premises to meet data residency requirements. This regional expansion provides additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that customers’ Outposts can connect to.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-07-27T21:50:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/07/aws-outposts-rack-supported-aws-asia-pacific-jakarta-region/","postDateTime":"2022-07-27T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts rack is now supported in the AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack is now supported in AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region. AWS Outposts rack is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-07-aws-outposts-rack-panama","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/07/aws-outposts-rack-panama/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:58:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Panama.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack, a part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts family\u003c/a\u003e, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any data center or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts rack is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, data residency, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts rack in Panama, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Outposts rack, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of AWS Regions where Outposts rack is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e. AWS partners can sign up for our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws-events.webex.com/mw3300/mywebex/default.do?nomenu\u003dtrue\u0026amp;siteurl\u003daws-events\u0026amp;service\u003d6\u0026amp;rnd\u003d0.9075859871119419\u0026amp;main_url\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Faws-events.webex.com%2Fec3300%2Feventcenter%2Fevent%2FeventAction.do%3FtheAction%3Ddetail%26%26%26EMK%3D4832534b00000005270092b3053bb9e0a4940bc201bcee96d898b0a7e9292fb311860ce38cfd3175%26siteurl%3Daws-events%26confViewID%3D231588697471990855%26encryptTicket%3DSDJTSwAAAAUjKCgrUDkFURQGJqP7c-Tk8mq-IAdsWJzl2PzNLpGJ6Q2%26\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eupcoming webinar\u003c/a\u003e to understand more about Outposts rack availability in Panama. The webinar will be delivered in Spanish.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-07-01T18:47:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/07/aws-outposts-rack-panama/","postDateTime":"2022-07-01T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts rack in Panama","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack can now be shipped and installed at your data center and on-premises locations in Panama.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-amazon-s3-outposts-presigned-urls","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-s3-outposts-presigned-urls/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:33:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports presigned URLs for granting time-limited access to objects stored locally on an Outpost. S3 on Outposts bucket owners can now more easily share objects with individuals in their Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePrior to presigned URLs, to share objects with other users, bucket owners would assign IAM policies to buckets. Now, with presigned URLs, bucket owners have a time-limited way to grant the ability to share, upload, or delete objects with other individuals in their VPC. Bucket owners can grant time-limited access with the presigned URL by choosing a custom expiration time that can be as low as one second and up to seven days, using the AWS CLI and SDKs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts rack environment to help you meet your low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. AWS Outposts rack, as part of the AWS Outposts Family, is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePresigned URLs are now available at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts rack is available\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with presigned URLs or learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e, or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/S3OutpostsPresignedURL.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-29T16:22:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-s3-outposts-presigned-urls/","postDateTime":"2022-06-29T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts now supports presigned URLs","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports presigned URLs for granting time-limited access to objects stored locally on an Outpost. S3 on Outposts bucket owners can now more easily share objects with individuals in their Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-amazon-ec2-placement-groups-support-host-level-spread-aws-outposts-rack","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-ec2-placement-groups-support-host-level-spread-aws-outposts-rack/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/placement-groups.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EC2 placement groups\u003c/a\u003e to spread instances across distinct hosts on an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts rack\u003c/a\u003e. Host-level spread placement groups distribute instances across hosts to reduce the likelihood of correlated failures, benefiting workloads that require High Availability (HA) like mission-critical databases.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts rack, a part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts family\u003c/a\u003e, is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises datacenter or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. When you create a spread placement group that will be used in an Outpost, you can set an optional Spread Level parameter to “rack” or “host”, which determines how instances are distributed across the underlying hardware. If no Spread Level is defined, “rack” is selected by default. Spreading instances across distinct hosts is useful in Outposts environments when you want to protect against host failures that can occur within a rack. The number of instances you can launch into a host-level spread placement group is limited only by the number of hosts available in your Outpost.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eHost-level spread placement groups are available to all Outposts customers at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where Outposts rack is supported. To learn more about AWS Outposts rack, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack product page\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about EC2 placement groups on Outposts, visit the Outposts user guide.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-28T21:05:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-ec2-placement-groups-support-host-level-spread-aws-outposts-rack/","postDateTime":"2022-06-28T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EC2 placement groups now support host-level spread on AWS Outposts rack","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/placement-groups.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EC2 placement groups\u003c/a\u003e to spread instances across distinct hosts on an \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts/rack.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts rack\u003c/a\u003e. Host-level spread placement groups distribute instances across hosts to reduce the likelihood of correlated failures, benefiting workloads that require High Availability (HA) like mission-critical databases.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-amazon-s3-outposts-aws-privatelink-buckets-access-points","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-s3-outposts-aws-privatelink-buckets-access-points/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:41:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now supports AWS PrivateLink, providing direct access to manage your S3 on Outposts storage capacity via a private endpoint within your virtual private network. This allows you to simplify your internal network architecture and perform management operations on your S3 storage by using private IP addresses in your Virtual Private Cloud (VPC), eliminating the need to use public IPs or proxy servers. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers today connect on-premises applications with Amazon S3 on Outposts using private IP addresses within their VPC, privately transferring object data in and out of S3 on Outposts. Many customers, however, also want to manage their S3 on Outposts capacity without configuring public IPs or proxy servers. With full S3 on Outposts support for PrivateLink, you can now provision interface VPC endpoints for the S3 on Outposts Control API in your VPC. This allows you to seamlessly create buckets, manage endpoints, and apply security policies from within your own VPC via the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI) or programmatically via AWS Software Development Kits (SDKs). Interface VPC endpoints are private endpoints that are assigned private IPs from your VPC.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises datacenter or co-location space for a truly consistent hybrid experience. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts rack environment to help you meet low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and your on-premises networks, without exposing your traffic to the public internet.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS PrivateLink is available at a low per-GB charge for data processed and a low hourly charge for interface VPC endpoints. For pricing details,\u0026nbsp;please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink pricing\u003c/a\u003e. You can get started by creating a PrivateLink interface endpoint for S3 on Outposts within your VPC using the AWS Management Console, AWS CLI, SDK, or AWS CloudFormation. Amazon S3 on Outposts, and support for PrivateLink, is available in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts rack is available\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with PrivateLink or learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e, or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-outposts-privatelink-interface-endpoints.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-01T18:44:47Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-s3-outposts-aws-privatelink-buckets-access-points/","postDateTime":"2022-06-01T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts now supports AWS PrivateLink for management of buckets and access points","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now supports AWS PrivateLink, providing direct access to manage your S3 on Outposts storage capacity via a private endpoint within your virtual private network. This allows you to simplify your internal network architecture and perform management operations on your S3 storage by using private IP addresses in your Virtual Private Cloud (VPC), eliminating the need to use public IPs or proxy servers. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-privatelink","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-privatelink","description":"general:products/aws-privatelink","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-amazon-ec2-dedicated-hosts-available-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-ec2-dedicated-hosts-available-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are announcing support for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/dedicated-hosts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) Dedicated Hosts\u003c/a\u003e on AWS Outposts, which makes it easier for customers to bring their existing software licenses and workloads that require a dedicated physical server to their Outpost Racks. In addition, customers now have greater flexibility in instance type deployment and more granular placement control, all with consistent hybrid experience on AWS Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts allow customers to use their eligible software licenses that are bound to VMs, sockets, or physical cores on EC2 instances, so that customers get the flexibility and cost effectiveness of using their own licenses. While Outposts has always been a single tenant environment eligible for Bring Your Own License (BYOL) workloads, Dedicated Hosts allows customers to limit licenses to a single host as opposed to the entire Outpost.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eDedicated Hosts on Outposts is also launching with multiple instance type support. When this support is selected, the Dedicated Host is able to launch different instance types (instance sizes) in the selected instance family. Instances can be launched without pre-planning the configuration of instance types, and utilization of the host can be monitored via the Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts console and API. Customers can launch instances onto a specific Dedicated Host or let Amazon EC2 place the instances automatically across Dedicated Hosts that they have configured on their Outpost. Controlling instance placement allows customers to address resiliency needs of mission critical applications. Dedicated Hosts can be shared using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM), which allows Outposts owners to distribute AWS accounts within their organization onto distinct hardware.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eDedicated Hosts on Outposts are available for all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/features/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EC2 instances available on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e and in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts Rack is supported\u003c/a\u003e. The support for Dedicated Hosts on Outposts is available at no additional cost. To learn more about Dedicated Hosts, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/dedicated-hosts-overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ethe EC2 Documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about AWS Outposts, visit this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/what-is-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ethe Outposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-01T15:30:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/amazon-ec2-dedicated-hosts-available-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2022-06-01T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts are now available on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we are announcing support for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/ec2/dedicated-hosts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) Dedicated Hosts\u003c/a\u003e on AWS Outposts, which makes it easier for customers to bring their existing software licenses and workloads that require a dedicated physical server to their Outpost Racks. In addition, customers now have greater flexibility in instance type deployment and more granular placement control, all with consistent hybrid experience on AWS Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-04-amazon-relational-database-service-multi-az-deployments-aws-outposts-high-availability","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/amazon-relational-database-service-multi-az-deployments-aws-outposts-high-availability/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports highly available configurations with Multi-AZ deployments for PostgreSQL and for MySQL on AWS Outposts in all commercial regions. Amazon RDS Multi-AZ on Outposts deployments provide enhanced availability and durability for RDS database (DB) instances, making them a natural fit for production database workloads. When you provision a Multi-AZ database instance, Amazon RDS automatically creates a primary DB Instance and synchronously replicates the data to a standby instance on a second AWS Outposts connected to a different \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regions_az/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAvailability Zone\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp; (AZ). Each Outposts runs on its own physically distinct, independent infrastructure, and is engineered to be highly reliable. In case of an infrastructure failure, Amazon RDS performs an automatic fail-over to the standby, so that you can resume database operations as soon as the fail-over is complete.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS Multi-AZ for MySQL and for PostgreSQL on Outposts deployments utilize synchronous physical replication to keep data on the standby up-to-date with the primary. They safeguard your data in the event of a DB Instance failure or failure of an Outpost. With Amazon RDS Multi-AZ on Outposts, I/O activity is not suspended on your primary during backup for Multi-AZ deployments because the backup is taken from the standby. If an Outposts failure or database instance failure occurs, your availability impact is limited. In the case of system upgrades like OS patching or DB Instance scaling, these operations are applied first on the standby, prior to an automatic fail-over. As a result, your availability impact is only the time required for automatic fail-over to complete.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS Multi-AZ on AWS Outposts is now available in all commercial regions where AWS Outposts are available. For more information about Amazon RDS on Outposts, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e, our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rds/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eget started\u003c/a\u003e now.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-04-20T16:39:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/amazon-relational-database-service-multi-az-deployments-aws-outposts-high-availability/","postDateTime":"2022-04-20T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Relational Database Service now supports Multi-AZ deployments on AWS Outposts for High Availability","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/rds.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports highly available configurations with Multi-AZ deployments for PostgreSQL and for MySQL on AWS Outposts in all commercial regions. Amazon RDS Multi-AZ on Outposts deployments provide enhanced availability and durability for RDS database (DB) instances, making them a natural fit for production database workloads. When you provision a Multi-AZ database instance, Amazon RDS automatically creates a primary DB Instance and synchronously replicates the data to a standby instance on a second AWS Outposts connected to a different \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regions_az.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAvailability Zone\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp; (AZ). Each Outposts runs on its own physically distinct, independent infrastructure, and is engineered to be highly reliable. In case of an infrastructure failure, Amazon RDS performs an automatic fail-over to the standby, so that you can resume database operations as soon as the fail-over is complete.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-04-aws-backup-support-vmware-cloud-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/aws-backup-support-vmware-cloud-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:47:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:27:58+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to protect VMware’s Software-Defined Data Centers (SDDC) on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vmware/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVMware Cloud on AWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e, helping you meet your business and regulatory compliance needs. You can use a single policy in AWS Backup to centrally automate data protection and lifecycle management of your on-premises VMware, VMware Cloud on AWS, and VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts environments alongside the 12 AWS services (spanning compute, storage, and databases) that AWS Backup supports.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup provides a consistent and fully managed data protection experience for your hybrid VMware workloads. VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts is a jointly-engineered solution with VMware that delivers VMware Cloud on AWS as a fully managed experience to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. Using AWS Backup, you can centrally configure data protection policies for VMware workloads hosted on your managed infrastructure, in VMware Cloud on AWS, and on VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts. You can restore your VMware backups to your on-premises data centers, in VMware Cloud on AWS, and on VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts to meet your application data recovery needs. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup for VMware is available in the US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (N. California, Oregon), AWS GovCloud (US-East, US-West), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Milan, Paris, Stockholm), South America (Sao Paulo), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong, Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo, Osaka), Middle East (Bahrain), and Africa (Cape Town) Regions. To learn more about AWS Backup for VMware, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/features/vmware\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/vm-backups.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/backup\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Backup console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-04-01T19:49:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/aws-backup-support-vmware-cloud-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2022-04-01T17:28:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Backup adds support for VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/backup.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to protect VMware’s Software-Defined Data Centers (SDDC) on \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/vmware/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVMware Cloud on AWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e, helping you meet your business and regulatory compliance needs. You can use a single policy in AWS Backup to centrally automate data protection and lifecycle management of your on-premises VMware, VMware Cloud on AWS, and VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts environments alongside the 12 AWS services (spanning compute, storage, and databases) that AWS Backup supports.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-backup","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-backup","description":"general:products/aws-backup","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-amazon-rds-postgresql-amazon-rds-outposts-postgresql-minor-versions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-rds-postgresql-amazon-rds-outposts-postgresql-minor-versions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:16:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eFollowing the announcement of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-141-135-129-1114-1019-and-9624-released-2349/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eupdates to the PostgreSQL database\u003c/a\u003e, we have added support in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/postgresql/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e for PostgreSQL minor versions 13.5, 12.9, 11.14, 10.19, and 9.6.24. We have also added support in Amazon RDS on Outposts for PostgreSQL minor versions 13.5 and 12.9. This release closes security vulnerabilities in PostgreSQL and contains bug fixes and improvements done by the PostgreSQL community. This also includes the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003efinal release of PostgreSQL 9.6\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS for PostgreSQL makes it easy to set up, operate, and scale PostgreSQL deployments in the cloud. Learn more about upgrading your database instances from the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_UpgradeDBInstance.Upgrading.html#USER_UpgradeDBInstance.PostgreSQL\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS User Guide\u003c/a\u003e. See \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/postgresql/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS for PostgreSQL Pricing\u003c/a\u003e for pricing details and regional availability. Create or update a fully managed Amazon RDS database in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/rds/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-24T18:15:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-rds-postgresql-amazon-rds-outposts-postgresql-minor-versions/","postDateTime":"2022-01-24T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL supports new minor versions 13.5, 12.9, 11.14, 10.19, and 9.6.24; Amazon RDS on Outposts supports new PostgreSQL minor versions 13.5 and 12.9","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eFollowing the announcement of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-141-135-129-1114-1019-and-9624-released-2349/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eupdates to the PostgreSQL database\u003c/a\u003e, we have added support in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/rds/postgresql.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e for PostgreSQL minor versions 13.5, 12.9, 11.14, 10.19, and 9.6.24. We have also added support in Amazon RDS on Outposts for PostgreSQL minor versions 13.5 and 12.9. This release closes security vulnerabilities in PostgreSQL and contains bug fixes and improvements done by the PostgreSQL community. This also includes the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003efinal release of PostgreSQL 9.6\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-aws-outposts-now-fedramp-authorized","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/aws-outposts-now-fedramp-authorized/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:23:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing AWS Outposts is now FedRAMP Moderate authorized for US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon) and FedRAMP High authorized for GovCloud (US-West) and GovCloud (US-East).\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any on-premises or edge location for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is available in a variety of form factors, from 1U and 2U Outposts servers to 42U Outposts racks. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and to effectively meet your data residency requirements. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFedRAMP granted authorization to AWS Outposts, excluding the hardware components of the service. This means customers and agencies can make a risk-based decision to use AWS Outposts hardware components or conduct a Type Accreditation to review the hardware components of AWS Outposts to process FedRAMP workloads. With this authorization for AWS Outposts for software, in conjunction with a risk-based decision by a federal authorizing official for hardware, customers in the U.S. Federal Agency Community can leverage FedRAMP authorized AWS services in on-premises and edge locations to run their workloads and store data per FedRAMP’s compliance requirements for cloud products and services.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-18T17:40:07Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/aws-outposts-now-fedramp-authorized/","postDateTime":"2022-01-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts now FedRAMP authorized","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing AWS Outposts is now FedRAMP Moderate authorized for US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon) and FedRAMP High authorized for GovCloud (US-West) and GovCloud (US-East).\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-12-amazon-s3-outposts-aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/12/amazon-s3-outposts-aws-govcloud-us/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:06:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is now available in both \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. The expansion into the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions allows U.S. government agencies and contractors to move sensitive workloads onto their AWS Outposts by addressing their specific regulatory and compliance requirements for object storage.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts helps you meet your low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs by delivering object storage to your Outpost on premises. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of all regions where S3 on Outposts is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts Region table\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about S3 on Outposts, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-12-22T17:49:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/12/amazon-s3-outposts-aws-govcloud-us/","postDateTime":"2021-12-22T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts launches in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is now available in both \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. The expansion into the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions allows U.S. government agencies and contractors to move sensitive workloads onto their AWS Outposts by addressing their specific regulatory and compliance requirements for object storage.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-aws-outposts-form-factors","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-outposts-form-factors/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:37:11+0000","additionalFields":{"modifiedDate":"2021-12-03T19:32:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-outposts-form-factors/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts 1U and 2U rack-mountable servers are now generally available.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe 1U server is 19“ wide, 24” deep, and is available with C6gd instances powered by Graviton2, with 64 vCPUs, 128 GiB memory, and 4 TB of local NVMe storage. The Outposts 2U server is 19“ wide, 30” deep, and is available with C6id instances powered with 3rd generation Intel Xeon Scalable processors, with up to 128 vCPUs, 256 GiB memory, and 8 TB of local NVMe storage. You can run Amazon EC2 instances for Virtual Machines, use VPC for networking, and run Amazon ECS for containers with support for Amazon EKS coming soon. Outposts server capacity can be managed by the same in-Region tools like Amazon CloudWatch, AWS CloudFormation, and AWS Code Deploy that you use to deploy applications in the AWS Region or to Outposts racks.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-aws-outposts-servers-in-two-form-factors/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","postDateTime":"2021-11-30T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts is Now Available in Two Smaller Form Factors"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-aws-outposts-new-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-outposts-new-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:22:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your datacenter and on-premises locations in Costa Rica, Ecuador, Morocco, Nigeria, and Vietnam.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, data residency, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in these countries, you can use AWS services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo find out more about AWS Outposts, sign up for our upcoming webinars: Costa Rica and Ecuador (in Spanish) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/LATAM-field-OE-AWS-Outposts-EC-CR-2021-reg-event.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecustomers\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/9169730581764595982\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epartners\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/vn-aws-outpost-launch-reg.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVietnam\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(in English). To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct overview\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. For the most updated list of AWS Regions where Outposts is supported, check out the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-30T01:31:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-outposts-new-regions/","postDateTime":"2021-11-29T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Costa Rica, Ecuador, Morocco, Nigeria, and Vietnam","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at your datacenter and on-premises locations in Costa Rica, Ecuador, Morocco, Nigeria, and Vietnam.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-amazon-rds-backups-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-rds-backups-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:15:26+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on AWS Outposts now supports creating backups locally on AWS Outposts with Amazon S3 support. You can create backups of your Amazon RDS databases running on AWS Outposts to the same Outpost or to the AWS Region of your Outpost, allowing you to maintain your data residency requirements while giving you flexibility for maintaining your data recovery solutions. CloudFormation support will be coming soon.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn your monthly bill, Amazon RDS backups to an Outpost are billed the same as backup storage in an AWS region. This means that there is no additional charge for backup storage, up to 100% of your total database storage, within a region including all of the Outposts you have associated with for that region.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS on Outposts Pricing\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;page and our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-on-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eRDS Outposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e. Get started backing up your Amazon RDS database instances on Outposts on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/rds/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-22T22:27:39Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-rds-backups-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2021-11-22T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts now supports backups on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on AWS Outposts now supports creating backups locally on AWS Outposts with Amazon S3 support. You can create backups of your Amazon RDS databases running on AWS Outposts to the same Outpost or to the AWS Region of your Outpost, allowing you to maintain your data residency requirements while giving you flexibility for maintaining your data recovery solutions. CloudFormation support will be coming soon.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-migration-to-aws#hybrid-architecture","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-migration-to-aws","name":"hybrid-architecture","description":"marketing:migration-to-aws/hybrid-architecture","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:37:02+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-amazon-s3-outposts-strong-consistency","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-s3-outposts-strong-consistency/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:19:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now delivers strong read-after-write and list-after-write consistency for any storage request at no additional cost.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts helps you meet your low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs by storing data on AWS Outposts. Using the S3 APIs and features, you can store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to data stored locally in S3 on Outposts buckets. Any request to S3 on Outposts storage is now strongly consistent. After a successful write of a new object or an overwrite of an existing object, any subsequent read request immediately receives the latest object. S3 also provides strong consistency for list operations, so after a write, you can immediately perform a listing of the objects in a bucket with all changes reflected.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAnalytics applications often require access to an S3 object immediately after a write. Without strong consistency, you would need to insert custom code into these applications, or provision databases to keep objects consistent with any changes in S3 across all objects. With this launch, S3 on Outposts object APIs are strongly consistent, and applications that require access to an object immediately after a write are able to do so directly, with no custom code required.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAll Amazon S3 on Outposts customers automatically receive strong consistency starting today, in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts is available\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about strong consistency for Amazon S3, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-s3-update-strong-read-after-write-consistency/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e and visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-18T23:08:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/amazon-s3-outposts-strong-consistency/","postDateTime":"2021-11-18T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts now delivers strong consistency automatically for all applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now delivers strong read-after-write and list-after-write consistency for any storage request at no additional cost.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-aws-rds-outposts-exporting-database-logs-amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-rds-outposts-exporting-database-logs-amazon-cloudwatch/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on AWS Outposts can now export database logs to Amazon CloudWatch. You can now monitor all of your Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts database instances from the same single pane of glass as your Amazon RDS database instances in our AWS Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon CloudWatch is a monitoring and observability service built for DevOps engineers, developers, and IT managers. CloudWatch provides you with data and actionable insights to monitor your applications, respond to system-wide performance changes, optimize resource utilization, and get a unified view of operational health. CloudWatch collects monitoring and operational data in the form of logs, metrics, traces, and events, providing you with a unified view of AWS resources, applications, and services that run on AWS and on-premises servers. You can use CloudWatch to help detect anomalous behavior in your environments, set alarms, visualize logs and metrics side by side, take automated actions, troubleshoot issues, and discover insights to keep your applications running smoothly.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn your monthly bill, Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts logs will incur the same charges as they do for RDS database logs in CloudWatch in an AWS region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Cloudwatch Pricing\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;page and our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-on-outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eRDS out Outposts documentation\u003c/a\u003e. Get started exporting your Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts database logs by following this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/premiumsupport/knowledge-center/rds-aurora-mysql-logs-cloudwatch/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehow-to\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-02T19:43:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-rds-outposts-exporting-database-logs-amazon-cloudwatch/","postDateTime":"2021-11-02T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts now supports exporting database logs to Amazon CloudWatch","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on AWS Outposts can now export database logs to Amazon CloudWatch. You can now monitor all of your Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts database instances from the same single pane of glass as your Amazon RDS database instances in our AWS Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-migration-to-aws#hybrid-architecture","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-migration-to-aws","name":"hybrid-architecture","description":"marketing:migration-to-aws/hybrid-architecture","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:37:02+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-10-amazon-rds-mysql-outposts-new-versions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/10/amazon-rds-mysql-outposts-new-versions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:13:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe have updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/mysql/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) for MySQL on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to support MySQL minor versions 8.0.23, and 8.0.25. We recommend that customers upgrade to the latest minor versions to fix known security vulnerabilities in prior versions of MySQL, and to benefit from the numerous bug fixes, performance improvements, and new functionality added by the MySQL community.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about upgrading your database instances in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_UpgradeDBInstance.MySQL.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS User Guide\u003c/a\u003e; and create or update a fully managed Amazon RDS database using the latest available minor versions in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/rds/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon RDS for MySQL on Outposts makes it easy to set up, operate, and scale MySQL deployments on premises and in the cloud. See \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon RDS for MySQL on Outposts Pricing\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for pricing details and regional availability. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-10-28T17:54:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/10/amazon-rds-mysql-outposts-new-versions/","postDateTime":"2021-10-20T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon RDS for MySQL on Outposts supports new minor versions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe have updated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/rds/mysql.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) for MySQL on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to support MySQL minor versions 8.0.23, and 8.0.25. We recommend that customers upgrade to the latest minor versions to fix known security vulnerabilities in prior versions of MySQL, and to benefit from the numerous bug fixes, performance improvements, and new functionality added by the MySQL community.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds-for-sql-server","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds-for-sql-server","description":"general:products/amazon-rds-for-sql-server","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-10-aws-outposts-cloudwatch-dimension-capacity-monitoring","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/10/aws-outposts-cloudwatch-dimension-capacity-monitoring/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:05:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing the availability of a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;dimension for metrics in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e namespace. CloudWatch dimensions are unique identifiers for metrics that allow customers to search and filter results.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn order to help Outposts customers gain visibility into what accounts and services are using the capacity in their Outposts deployment, we’ve added the Account dimension to the following Outposts metrics:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eInstanceFamilyCapacityUtilization\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eInstanceTypeCapacityUtilization\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eUsedInstanceType_Count\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eOutposts customers can now create alarms to be triggered when utilization of a specific instance type or family reach conditions they specify on a per account or per service basis.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCloudWatch metrics for AWS Outposts are available to customers in all public AWS Regions and AWS GovCloud (US) at no additional cost. You can start using these metrics through the AWS Management Console, AWS CLI, or AWS SDK. To learn more, visit the AWS Outposts \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-cloudwatch-metrics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To learn best practices for planning, monitoring, and managing capacity with AWS Outposts, join \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/AWS-Online-Tech-Talks_October-2021.html?webinar\u003d2021_1011-CMP\u0026amp;trk\u003del_a134p000007CaadAAC\u0026amp;trkCampaign\u003dCOMPUTE-OUTPOSTS-HYBDCLD-SOL-October_2021_1011-CMP\u0026amp;sc_channel\u003del\u0026amp;sc_campaign\u003dpac_Q4-2021_exlinks_PMM_OTT_10DGAB\u0026amp;sc_outcome\u003dProduct_Adoption_Campaigns\u0026amp;sc_geo\u003dNAMER\u0026amp;sc_country\u003dmult\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ethis webinar\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-10-13T21:36:47Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/10/aws-outposts-cloudwatch-dimension-capacity-monitoring/","postDateTime":"2021-10-13T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts adds new CloudWatch dimension for capacity monitoring","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing the availability of a new \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudwatch.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;dimension for metrics in the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e namespace. CloudWatch dimensions are unique identifiers for metrics that allow customers to search and filter results.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-10-general-availability-vmware-cloud-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/10/general-availability-vmware-cloud-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:24:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are announcing the general availability of VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts, a jointly-engineered solution that delivers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vmware/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVMware Cloud on AWS\u003c/a\u003e as a fully managed experience to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. It runs VMware’s enterprise-class Software-Defined Data Center (SDDC) software on dedicated AWS Nitro System-based EC2 bare metal Outposts instances. VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts is built for VMware workloads that require low-latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, or data residency.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVMware Cloud on AWS Outposts simplifies IT operations. AWS delivers and installs the Outpost at your on-premises location, monitors, patches, and updates it, and handles all maintenance and replacement of the hardware. VMware provides continuous lifecycle management of VMware SDDC and serves as your first line of support.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVMware Cloud on AWS and VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts share the same infrastructure, architecture, and operations, offering a truly consistent hybrid experience. With access to over 200 AWS services, VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts empowers you to innovate faster wherever your workloads need to be deployed.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts, you can contact your AWS or VMware sales representative to place an order. VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts can be shipped to the US and connected to US East (N. Virginia) or US West (Oregon). If you want to deploy VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts outside of the US or connect VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts to other AWS regions, please contact your AWS or VMware sales representative.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vmware/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/vmware-cloud-on-aws-outposts-brings-vmware-sddc-as-a-fully-managed-service-on-premises\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-10-05T17:44:13Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/10/general-availability-vmware-cloud-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2021-10-05T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing general availability of VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are announcing the general availability of VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts, a jointly-engineered solution that delivers \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/vmware.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVMware Cloud on AWS\u003c/a\u003e as a fully managed experience to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. It runs VMware’s enterprise-class Software-Defined Data Center (SDDC) software on dedicated AWS Nitro System-based EC2 bare metal Outposts instances. VMware Cloud on AWS Outposts is built for VMware workloads that require low-latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, or data residency.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-08-amazon-s3-outposts-supports-sharing-across-multiple-accounts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/amazon-s3-outposts-supports-sharing-across-multiple-accounts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:18:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports sharing of S3 capacity across multiple accounts within an organization using AWS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ram/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eResource Access Manager\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(RAM). Multiple teams within your organization can now create and manage buckets, access points, and endpoints on S3 on Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts environment to help you meet your low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eNow with support for RAM, S3 on Outposts resource management can be streamlined to help reduce operational overhead, provide consistency for sharing resources, and visibility into shared accounts usage. RAM is designed to create a resource share where you specify the resources, principal, and the associated managed permissions. Principals can be an organization or organizational units (OUs) in AWS Organizations, AWS accounts, IAM roles, and IAM users.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts, and support for sharing across multiple accounts, is available in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts is available\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e , or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-08-05T18:45:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/amazon-s3-outposts-supports-sharing-across-multiple-accounts/","postDateTime":"2021-08-05T18:28:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts now supports sharing across multiple accounts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports sharing of S3 capacity across multiple accounts within an organization using AWS \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/ram.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eResource Access Manager\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(RAM). Multiple teams within your organization can now create and manage buckets, access points, and endpoints on S3 on Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-amazon-s3-outposts-adds-two-larger-storage-tiers","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/amazon-s3-outposts-adds-two-larger-storage-tiers/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now offers two larger storage tiers: 240 TB and 380 TB.  These new storage tiers help you meet your needs for workloads with larger object storage requirements, and add to the existing options of: 26 TB, 48 TB, and 96 TB storage tiers.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eS3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts environment to help you meet low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. These two new S3 storage tiers deliver additional flexibility to enable you to tailor S3 storage on Outposts to meet the demands of larger workloads.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts, and the new larger storage tiers, is available in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts is available\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit the S3 on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eOutposts page\u003c/a\u003e, or see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-29T19:03:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/amazon-s3-outposts-adds-two-larger-storage-tiers/","postDateTime":"2021-07-29T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts adds two larger storage tiers","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now offers two larger storage tiers: 240 TB and 380 TB.  These new storage tiers help you meet your needs for workloads with larger object storage requirements, and add to the existing options of: 26 TB, 48 TB, and 96 TB storage tiers.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-amazon-s3-outposts-supports-direct-access-applications-running-outside-outposts-vpc","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/amazon-s3-outposts-supports-direct-access-applications-running-outside-outposts-vpc/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports the ability to create and access S3 objects on Outposts directly from your on-premises network. You can now configure S3 endpoints using your\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-networking-components.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecustomer owned IP\u003c/a\u003e (CoIP) addresses and access your S3 objects from your on-premise network through the Outposts\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-networking-components.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLocal Gateway\u003c/a\u003e (LGW).\u0026nbsp;With direct access, applications outside the Outposts Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) can now directly access data stored in S3 buckets on your Outposts.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts environment to help you meet low latency, local data processing, and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easier to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outposts. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts is available in all AWS Regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts is available\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eS3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;page, or see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-29T18:44:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/amazon-s3-outposts-supports-direct-access-applications-running-outside-outposts-vpc/","postDateTime":"2021-07-29T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts supports direct access for applications running outside the Outposts VPC","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/s3/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts\u003c/a\u003e now supports the ability to create and access S3 objects on Outposts directly from your on-premises network. You can now configure S3 endpoints using your\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-networking-components.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecustomer owned IP\u003c/a\u003e (CoIP) addresses and access your S3 objects from your on-premise network through the Outposts\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-networking-components.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLocal Gateway\u003c/a\u003e (LGW).\u0026nbsp;With direct access, applications outside the Outposts Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) can now directly access data stored in S3 buckets on your Outposts.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-amazon-ec2-placement-groups-are-now-available-on-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/amazon-ec2-placement-groups-are-now-available-on-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:45:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) placement groups allow you to influence the placement strategy of instances on the underlying hardware. You can select from cluster, spread or partition placement strategies, depending on the needs of the workload.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon EC2 placement groups on Outposts, you can now use the spread and partition placement strategies to improve the resilience of workloads configured for high availability. A spread placement group places each instance of the group on a distinct rack to reduce correlated failures. A partition placement group distributes instances across logical partitions such that groups of instances in one partition do not share a rack with instances of a different partition.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EC2 placement groups on Outposts are available to all Outposts customers at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where Outposts is supported today. For more information about EC2 spread placement groups, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/placement-groups.html#placement-groups-spread\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eour documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-28T22:41:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/amazon-ec2-placement-groups-are-now-available-on-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2021-07-28T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EC2 Placement Groups are now available on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) placement groups allow you to influence the placement strategy of instances on the underlying hardware. You can select from cluster, spread or partition placement strategies, depending on the needs of the workload.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-announcing-availability-aws-outposts-argentina-chile-peru","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/announcing-availability-aws-outposts-argentina-chile-peru/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:15:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at\u0026nbsp;your datacenter and on-premises locations in Argentina*, Chile, and Peru.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, data residency, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in these three additional countries, you can leverage AWS Services to run your workloads and data in country in your on-premises facilities and connect to your nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo find out more about AWS Outposts in Argentina, Chile, and Peru, sign up for our upcoming \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/LATAM-field-OE-Outposts-Launch-CL-ARG-2021-reg-event.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ewebinar for AWS customers\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://register.gotowebinar.com/register/7599282727832983051\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ewebinar for AWS partners\u003c/a\u003e. The webinars will be delivered in Spanish. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e*\u0026nbsp;AWS Outposts in Argentina will be available in Buenos Aires and Santa Fe provinces with support for additional provinces coming soon.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-28T17:19:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/announcing-availability-aws-outposts-argentina-chile-peru/","postDateTime":"2021-07-28T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Argentina, Chile, and Peru","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at\u0026nbsp;your datacenter and on-premises locations in Argentina*, Chile, and Peru.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-06-aws-outposts-is-now-supported-in-aws-asia-pacific-osaka-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/aws-outposts-is-now-supported-in-aws-asia-pacific-osaka-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:39+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility.  Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, data residency, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eOrganizations from startups to enterprise and the public sector in and outside of Japan can now connect Outposts to the AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region. AWS Outposts enables customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to the AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region for application management. You can also use Outposts and AWS Services to manage and process data that remain on premises to meet data residency requirements. With this regional expansion, both AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region and AWS Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Region in Japan now support Outposts, providing additional flexibility in the AWS Regions that your Outposts can connect to. In addition, you can now have multiple logical Outposts connected to Availability Zones (AZs) in different AWS Regions within Japan for high availability configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-23T19:23:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/aws-outposts-is-now-supported-in-aws-asia-pacific-osaka-region/","postDateTime":"2021-06-23T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts is now supported in AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility.  Outposts is ideal for workloads that require low latency access to on-premises systems, local data processing, data residency, and migration of applications with local system interdependencies.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-aws-outposts-launches-support-for-ec2-capacity-reservations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-outposts-launches-support-for-ec2-capacity-reservations/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:57:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can create and manage reserved capacity on Amazon EC2 instances on your Outposts. You can also share the Capacity Reservations on Outposts with other AWS accounts within your organization. With Capacity Reservations on Outposts, you can ensure that you always have access to EC2 capacity when you need it, for as long as you need it.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can choose from a variety of AWS Outposts configurations, each providing a wide selection of EC2 instance types where they can run their applications. Some customers however have very specific requirements for portions of their applications around instance type, size, and capability, and need very high levels of assurance that they will always be able to launch that specific capacity on Outposts. Now with Capacity Reservations on Outposts, customers can create and manage capacity reservations centrally, and also share the reserved capacity on Outposts with other AWS accounts, within an organization, using AWS Resource Access Manager. This is ideal for customers who want to ensure that their application has resources for future increases in demand, including planned or unplanned spikes, backup and disaster recovery, or for planned growth and buffer.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can create, modify, and remove capacity reservation on Outposts at any time using the AWS Management Console, AWS SDK and CLI. To get started, use the create-capacity-reservation command with these attributes: Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Outpost, Instance Type - the type of instance to launch into the reserved capacity, and Instance Count - the number of instances for which to reserve capacity. For example, the following command creates a Capacity Reservation that reserves capacity for five m5.2xlarge in an Outpost.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e$aws ec2 create-capacity-reservation --outpost-id op-8d7d65e20146a962e --instance-type m5.2xlarge --instance-count 5\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo share the Capacity Reservations on Outposts with other AWS account within your organization follow these three easy steps: create a Resource Share through AWS Resource Access Manager, add resources (Capacity Reservations) to the Resource Share, and specify the target accounts that you wish to share the resources with. You can monitor the Capacity Reservations usage metrics using Amazon CloudWatch metrics and identify unused capacity by setting CloudWatch alarms to notify you when usage thresholds are met.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCapacity Reservations on Outposts are available to all Outposts customers at no additional cost and supported in all commercial and GovCloud regions and countries where Outposts is available today. To learn more about creating, managing, and sharing EC2 capacity reservations on Outposts, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/concepts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etechnical documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about AWS Outposts, visit this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-25T16:35:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-outposts-launches-support-for-ec2-capacity-reservations/","postDateTime":"2021-05-24T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts launches support for EC2 Capacity Reservations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can create and manage reserved capacity on Amazon EC2 instances on your Outposts. You can also share the Capacity Reservations on Outposts with other AWS accounts within your organization. With Capacity Reservations on Outposts, you can ensure that you always have access to EC2 capacity when you need it, for as long as you need it.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-announcing-postgresql-12-5-support-for-amazon-rds-on-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/announcing-postgresql-12-5-support-for-amazon-rds-on-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e on AWS Outposts now supports PostgreSQL 12.5 for production deployment. Amazon RDS on Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. You can deploy Amazon RDS on Outposts to set up, operate, and scale MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server and PostgreSQL relational databases on-premises, just as you would in the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS on Outposts can now deploy PostgreSQL 12.2, 12.3, 12.4, and 12.5. For more information about Amazon RDS on Outposts, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e, our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rds/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eget started\u003c/a\u003e now.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-14T19:53:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/announcing-postgresql-12-5-support-for-amazon-rds-on-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2021-05-14T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing PostgreSQL 12.5 support for Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/rds.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e on AWS Outposts now supports PostgreSQL 12.5 for production deployment. Amazon RDS on Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. You can deploy Amazon RDS on Outposts to set up, operate, and scale MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server and PostgreSQL relational databases on-premises, just as you would in the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-announcing-amazon-rds-for-sql-server-on-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/announcing-amazon-rds-for-sql-server-on-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS for SQL Server on AWS Outposts is now available to all AWS Outposts customers. Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon RDS for SQL Server on Outposts, you can run Microsoft SQL Server 2016, 2017, and 2019 in Enterprise, Standard and Web Editions. Amazon RDS for SQL Server on Outposts automates time-consuming administration tasks such as hardware provisioning, database setup, patching, and backups, and you can use your existing VPC connection, and the same Application Programmatic Interfaces (APIs) as you use in AWS today, which frees you to focus on your applications so you can give them the fast performance, high availability, security, and compatibility they need.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFind out more on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon RDS on AWS Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-create-microsoft-sql-server-instances-of-amazon-rds-on-aws-outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog on how to get started\u003c/a\u003e today.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-11T19:50:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/announcing-amazon-rds-for-sql-server-on-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2021-05-11T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing Amazon RDS for SQL Server on AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS for SQL Server on AWS Outposts is now available to all AWS Outposts customers. Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds-for-sql-server","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds-for-sql-server","description":"general:products/amazon-rds-for-sql-server","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-announcing-availability-aws-outposts-colombia-macao-puerto-rico","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/announcing-availability-aws-outposts-colombia-macao-puerto-rico/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:42:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in Colombia, Macao, and Puerto Rico.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet your data residency requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in these three additional countries and territories, customers can leverage AWS Services to run their workloads and data in country in their on-premises facilities and connect to their nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-05T16:59:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/announcing-availability-aws-outposts-colombia-macao-puerto-rico/","postDateTime":"2021-05-05T16:05:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Colombia, Macao, and Puerto Rico","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in Colombia, Macao, and Puerto Rico.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-in-the-philippines-and-brunei","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-in-the-philippines-and-brunei/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:42:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in the Philippines and Brunei.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet your data residency requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in the Philippines and Brunei, customers can leverage AWS Services to run their workloads and data in country in their on-premises facilities and connect to their nearest AWS Region for management and operations.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-21T16:06:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-in-the-philippines-and-brunei/","postDateTime":"2021-04-21T17:11:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in the Philippines and Brunei","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in the Philippines and Brunei.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-amazon-s3-on-outposts-events-now-available-in-amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-s3-on-outposts-events-now-available-in-amazon-cloudwatch/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:58:18+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now supports the ability to monitor your S3 on Outposts events via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e. You can now use CloudWatch Events to create a rule for any S3 on Outposts API Event to get notified via all supported CloudWatch targets such as Amazon SNS and Amazon SQS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts environment to help you meet local data processing and data residency needs. Using the Amazon S3 APIs and features, Amazon S3 on Outposts makes it easy to store and manage data on your AWS Outposts in your on-premises environment.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eCloudWatch console\u003c/a\u003e, CloudWatch CLI, or AWS SDK to start consuming Amazon S3 on Outposts events. To learn more about S3 on Outposts CloudWatch Events, review the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MonitoringS3Outposts.html#S3OutpostsNotificationsCWE\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. This feature is available in all AWS Regions where AWS Outposts is available. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon S3 on Outposts, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-27T00:18:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-s3-on-outposts-events-now-available-in-amazon-cloudwatch/","postDateTime":"2021-04-20T18:19:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts Events now available in Amazon CloudWatch","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts now supports the ability to monitor your S3 on Outposts events via \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudwatch.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e. You can now use CloudWatch Events to create a rule for any S3 on Outposts API Event to get notified via all supported CloudWatch targets such as Amazon SNS and Amazon SQS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-customer-owned-ip-generally-available-amazon-rds-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/customer-owned-ip-generally-available-amazon-rds-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:19+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomer owned IP (CoIP) addresses are now available for use with Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. CoIP allows you to assign addresses from your local network to services running on your AWS Outposts. Support for CoIP makes it easier to access your Amazon RDS databases from your local network using your own IPs. Amazon RDS on Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. You can deploy Amazon RDS on Outposts to set up, operate, and scale MySQL and PostgreSQL relational databases on premises, just as you would in the cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/latest/userguide/outposts-networking-components.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts networking\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon RDS on Outposts, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e, our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rds/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eget started\u003c/a\u003e now.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-23T18:05:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/customer-owned-ip-generally-available-amazon-rds-outposts/","postDateTime":"2020-12-23T12:55:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Customer Owned IP generally available for Amazon RDS on Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomer owned IP (CoIP) addresses are now available for use with Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS) on \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. CoIP allows you to assign addresses from your local network to services running on your AWS Outposts. Support for CoIP makes it easier to access your Amazon RDS databases from your local network using your own IPs. Amazon RDS on Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. You can deploy Amazon RDS on Outposts to set up, operate, and scale MySQL and PostgreSQL relational databases on premises, just as you would in the cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-new-versions-mysql-postgresql-available-amazon-rds-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/new-versions-mysql-postgresql-available-amazon-rds-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e on AWS Outposts now supports additional production ready versions of MySQL (8.0.19, 8.0.20, 8.0.21) and PostgreSQL (12.3, 12.4) for deployment. Amazon RDS on Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. You can deploy Amazon RDS on Outposts to set up, operate, and scale MySQL and PostgreSQL relational databases on-premises, just as you would in the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon RDS on Outposts can now deploy MySQL versions 8.0.17, 8.0.19, 8.0.20, 8.0.21 and PostgreSQL 12.2, 12.3, 12.4. For more information about Amazon RDS on Outposts, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e, our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rds/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/rds/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eget started\u003c/a\u003e now.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-23T22:04:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/new-versions-mysql-postgresql-available-amazon-rds-outposts/","postDateTime":"2020-12-23T12:36:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New versions of MySQL and PostgreSQL now available on Amazon RDS for Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/rds.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS)\u003c/a\u003e on AWS Outposts now supports additional production ready versions of MySQL (8.0.19, 8.0.20, 8.0.21) and PostgreSQL (12.3, 12.4) for deployment. Amazon RDS on Outposts allows you to deploy fully managed database instances in your on-premises environments. \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. You can deploy Amazon RDS on Outposts to set up, operate, and scale MySQL and PostgreSQL relational databases on-premises, just as you would in the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-announcing-the-availability-of-aws-outposts-private-connectivity","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/announcing-the-availability-of-aws-outposts-private-connectivity/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now connect your on-premises AWS Outposts infrastructure privately over Direct Connect to services running in the AWS region using AWS Outposts Private Connectivity. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts infrastructure installed at customer locations require a service link VPN connection to the parent AWS region for carrying control, management, and customer VPC traffic. Until now you had to connect the service link VPN to public endpoints (IPs) in the AWS region. With AWS Outposts Private Connectivity, you can now use your private VPC to connect your Outposts service link VPN to the parent AWS region. This minimizes exposure to the public internet and obviates the need for special firewall configurations for connectivity to AWS region.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou get improved data security as data and traffic move through the service link by leveraging your own VPCs and Direct Connect, helping you meet your stringent data security requirements. Private connectivity removes operational overhead required to change firewall configurations to accommodate public IPs, such as multiple approvals and tight coordination between IT and security teams.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Outposts Private Connectivity and to learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/outposts\"\u003eAWS Outposts website\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\"\u003eFAQs\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/console/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-21T22:56:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/announcing-the-availability-of-aws-outposts-private-connectivity/","postDateTime":"2020-12-21T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing the availability of AWS Outposts Private Connectivity ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now connect your on-premises AWS Outposts infrastructure privately over Direct Connect to services running in the AWS region using AWS Outposts Private Connectivity. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-aws-managed-services-ams-supports-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-managed-services-ams-supports-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Managed Services (AMS) can now operate AWS workloads hosted on AWS Outposts in your datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises environment. You can accelerate your migration to the cloud with AMS managed IT services for AWS Outposts hosted resources, including incident, problem, patch, and security management. AMS takes responsibility for managing AWS Outposts and resources hosted on AWS Outposts while providing a simple API for provisioning new capacity, requesting changes, and reporting incidents.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to providing operational support for workloads hosted on AWS Outposts, AMS is available in 15 additional AWS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e. Learn more about AMS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/managed-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e, and the SLAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ams.contract.docs/AWS+Managed+Services+Service+Level+Agreement.pdf\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-02T20:16:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-managed-services-ams-supports-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2020-12-02T12:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Managed Services (AMS) supports AWS Outposts ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Managed Services (AMS) can now operate AWS workloads hosted on AWS Outposts in your datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises environment. You can accelerate your migration to the cloud with AMS managed IT services for AWS Outposts hosted resources, including incident, problem, patch, and security management. AMS takes responsibility for managing AWS Outposts and resources hosted on AWS Outposts while providing a simple API for provisioning new capacity, requesting changes, and reporting incidents.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-managed-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-managed-services","description":"general:products/aws-managed-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-amazon-ebs-csi-driver-now-supports-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-ebs-csi-driver-now-supports-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) CSI driver now supports creating volumes on worker nodes running in AWS Outposts subnets. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that offers the same AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience The EBS CSI driver makes it easy to provision, attach, and mount EBS volumes into Kubernetes pods. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the latest release of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-ebs-csi-driver\"\u003eEBS CSI driver\u003c/a\u003e, you can dynamically provision EBS volumes for pods running in AWS Outposts subnets. This release also includes support for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-ebs-volume-type-io2-more-iops-gib-higher-durability/\"\u003eIO2 volume types\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/graviton/\"\u003eAWS Graviton\u003c/a\u003e based instance types. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-ebs-csi-driver/blob/master/CHANGELOG-0.x.md#v070\"\u003erelease notes\u003c/a\u003e for full details, and the Amazon EKS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/ebs-csi.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e to get started. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-07T21:52:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-ebs-csi-driver-now-supports-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2020-10-07T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EBS CSI driver now supports AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) CSI driver now supports creating volumes on worker nodes running in AWS Outposts subnets. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-block-store","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-block-store","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-block-store","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-amazon-s3-on-outposts-is-now-generally-available-expanding-object-storage-to-on-premises-environments","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-s3-on-outposts-is-now-generally-available-expanding-object-storage-to-on-premises-environments/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts environment to meet local data processing and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easy to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outpost. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo start using S3 on Outposts, visit the AWS Outposts Management Console to order an Outposts configuration that includes your desired S3 storage capacity, or you can add S3 storage to an existing Outpost by working with your AWS account team. You then use the AWS console or S3 SDK, or CLI to create buckets and S3 Access Points on your Outposts. You can control access and monitor your S3 on Outposts using the same services that you use with Amazon S3 today, such as AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), S3 Access Points and policies to control access to objects and buckets, Amazon CloudWatch to monitor operational health, and AWS CloudTrail to track and report on bucket-level activity. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts is now available in all AWS commercial regions where AWS Outposts is available. Please refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/faqs/\"\u003eAWS Outposts FAQs\u003c/a\u003e for S3 on Outposts availability. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/outposts/\"\u003eS3 on Outposts page\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/S3onOutposts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-s3-on-outposts-now-available\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-30T23:35:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-s3-on-outposts-is-now-generally-available-expanding-object-storage-to-on-premises-environments/","postDateTime":"2020-09-30T19:12:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon S3 on Outposts is now generally available, expanding object storage to on-premises environments","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon S3 on Outposts delivers object storage to your on-premises AWS Outposts environment to meet local data processing and data residency needs. Using the S3 APIs and features, S3 on Outposts makes it easy to store, secure, tag, retrieve, report on, and control access to the data on your Outpost. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, services, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-datasync","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-datasync","description":"general:products/aws-datasync","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-aws-outposts-ready-partners","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/aws-outposts-ready-partners/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/partners/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts Ready Program\u003c/a\u003e, part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/partners/service-ready/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Ready Program\u003c/a\u003e, help customers find integrated storage, networking, security, and industry-specific solutions that are validated by AWS experts to integrate with AWS Outposts deployments. AWS customers use AWS Outposts to benefit from the same AWS hardware infrastructure, services, APIs, and tools to build and run their applications on premises and in the cloud for a truly consistent hybrid experience. With AWS Outposts, customers can run AWS services locally on their Outpost, including EC2, EBS, ECS, EKS, and RDS, and also have full access to services available in the Region. Customers using specific tools and applications want to know which AWS Technology Partner products will help them to simplify and protect their AWS Outposts deployment, or accelerate access to insights on AWS Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProducts from AWS Outposts Ready Partners have been tested to run on AWS Outposts, enabling customers to easily identify products that will integrate with their AWS Outposts deployments. AWS Outposts Ready products are generally available and supported for AWS customers, with clear deployment documentation for AWS Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, see the following resources:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/partners/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts Ready Partner\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/apn/simplify-and-protect-your-outposts-deployment-and-accelerate-access-to-insights-with-aws-partner-solutions/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLearn more about this on APN blog post\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-15T16:29:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/aws-outposts-ready-partners/","postDateTime":"2020-09-15T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing AWS Outposts Ready Partners","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts/partners.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Outposts Ready Program\u003c/a\u003e, part of the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/partners/service-ready.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Ready Program\u003c/a\u003e, help customers find integrated storage, networking, security, and industry-specific solutions that are validated by AWS experts to integrate with AWS Outposts deployments. AWS customers use AWS Outposts to benefit from the same AWS hardware infrastructure, services, APIs, and tools to build and run their applications on premises and in the cloud for a truly consistent hybrid experience. With AWS Outposts, customers can run AWS services locally on their Outpost, including EC2, EBS, ECS, EKS, and RDS, and also have full access to services available in the Region. Customers using specific tools and applications want to know which AWS Technology Partner products will help them to simplify and protect their AWS Outposts deployment, or accelerate access to insights on AWS Outposts.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing#migration-to-aws","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing","name":"migration-to-aws","description":"marketing:migration-to-aws","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:33+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#partner#partner-level","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#partner","name":"partner-level","description":"partner:partner-level","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:00+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-in-nine-additional-countries-in-africa-asia-pacific-latin-america-and-middle-east","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-in-nine-additional-countries-in-africa-asia-pacific-latin-america-and-middle-east/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:04:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in Brazil, India, Israel, Malaysia, Mexico, New Zealand, South Africa, Taiwan, and Thailand, and supported in three additional Regions: AWS Africa (Cape Town) Region, Asia Pacific (Mumbai) Region, and South America (São Paulo) Region.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet your data residency requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in these nine additional countries, customers can leverage AWS Services to run their workloads and data in country in their on-premises facilities and connect to their nearest AWS Region for management and operations. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-06-24T17:27:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-in-nine-additional-countries-in-africa-asia-pacific-latin-america-and-middle-east/","postDateTime":"2020-06-24T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in nine additional countries in Africa, Asia Pacific, Latin America, and Middle East","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in Brazil, India, Israel, Malaysia, Mexico, New Zealand, South Africa, Taiwan, and Thailand, and supported in three additional Regions: AWS Africa (Cape Town) Region, Asia Pacific (Mumbai) Region, and South America (São Paulo) Region.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-aws-outposts-supported-aws-europe-milan-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/aws-outposts-supported-aws-europe-milan-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:04:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in AWS Europe (Milan) Region. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent AWS experience. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet your data residency requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eItalian organizations from startups to enterprise and the public sector can now connect Outposts to the AWS Europe (Milan) Region. AWS Outposts enables customers to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to the AWS Europe (Milan) Region for application management. They can also use Outposts and AWS Services to manage and process data that remain on premises. To see a complete list of AWS services available in the AWS Europe (Milan) Region please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-26T19:59:28Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/aws-outposts-supported-aws-europe-milan-region/","postDateTime":"2020-05-26T10:14:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts is now supported in AWS Europe (Milan) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in AWS Europe (Milan) Region. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent AWS experience. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet your data residency requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-announcing-price-reduction-for-aws-outposts-in-bahrain","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/announcing-price-reduction-for-aws-outposts-in-bahrain/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:02:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, pricing for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e general purpose, compute optimized, and memory optimized configurations has been reduced in the country of Bahrain. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou will save up to 11% depending on the Outposts configuration. For instance, the No Upfront monthly price for OR-HUZEI16 (our general purpose configuration for compute intensive applications) is now $28,539.47, reduced from $31,113.67.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about AWS Outposts configurations and pricing for different countries, visit the\u0026nbsp;visit the AWS Outposts \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable width\u003d\"1051\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\"\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"42\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eCategory\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eResource ID\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eNew Monthly Price (No Upfront)\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e\u003cb\u003ePrice Reduction\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eCompute Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-ODKC70D\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$24,250.75\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e9.82%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eCompute Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-REM3UIH\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$23,408.45\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e8.69%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eCompute Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-P7M7Y0S\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$15,685.75\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e6.45%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eCompute Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-OLB5RGB\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$15,264.60\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e5.42%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGeneral Purpose\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-KPUCKWN\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$25,935.34\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e11.78%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGeneral Purpose\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-SRG6JS4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$16,528.04\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e8.28%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGeneral Purpose\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-HUZEI16\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$28,539.47\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e8.27%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGeneral Purpose\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-LR4DI6P\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$27,046.14\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e8.10%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGeneral Purpose\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-OR2XU7Y\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$15,896.32\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e6.93%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGeneral Purpose\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-R2XVM9Q\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$17,408.96\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e4.61%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eGraphics Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-H7KSNNO\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$23,132.35\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e7.57%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eMemory Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-HSZHMMF\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$33,747.73\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e2.31%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"167\" height\u003d\"21\"\u003eMemory Optimized\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"104\"\u003eOR-MJV0E2L\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"225\"\u003e$20,434.24\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"111\"\u003e0.77%\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-18T19:45:28Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/announcing-price-reduction-for-aws-outposts-in-bahrain/","postDateTime":"2020-05-18T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing price reduction for AWS Outposts in Bahrain ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, pricing for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/outposts.html\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e general purpose, compute optimized, and memory optimized configurations has been reduced in the country of Bahrain. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-united-arab-emirates","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-united-arab-emirates/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in United Arab Emirates (UAE).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent AWS experience. Outposts is ideal for applications that need to run on-premises to meet low latency requirements. You can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet your data residency requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the availability of Outposts in UAE, customers can leverage AWS Services to run their workloads and data in country in their on-premises facilities and connect to any AWS Region for management and operations. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Outposts customers can run applications locally to meet low latency requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003csup\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003cb\u003eUpdated On: June 9, 2023. This post has been updated to remove Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA) from 1) the body of the post, and 2) the URL. As of this date, Outposts availability is pending authorization by KSA. Visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/rack/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts rack FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/servers/faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOutposts servers FAQs page\u003c/a\u003e for the most updated list of countries and territories where Outposts is currently available.\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-06-09T16:59:15Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/announcing-availability-of-aws-outposts-united-arab-emirates/","postDateTime":"2020-05-18T09:26:34Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in United Arab Emirates and Kingdom of Saudi Arabia","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in United Arab Emirates (UAE).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-announcing-availability-aws-outposts-indonesia","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/announcing-availability-aws-outposts-indonesia/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in Indonesia.  AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent AWS experience. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the new Indonesia country availability for Outposts, customers can leverage AWS Services to run their workloads and data in their on-premises facilities in Indonesia and connect to the nearest AWS Region such as the AWS Singapore Region for management and operations. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Outposts, customers can run applications on premises in order to meet low latency requirements. They can also use Outposts to process and manage data locally and effectively meet their compliance and data privacy requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-27T16:26:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/announcing-availability-aws-outposts-indonesia/","postDateTime":"2020-04-27T10:57:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing availability of AWS Outposts in Indonesia","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed at customer datacenters and on-premises locations in Indonesia.  AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent AWS experience. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-aws-outposts-is-now-supported-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/aws-outposts-is-now-supported-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:18+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS GovCloud (US) Regions are designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for public and private sector customers that have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFederal, state, and local government agencies, and commercial customers in regulated industries can now connect their Outposts to AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. With Outposts they can use AWS Services to process data and run applications in on-premises locations that they own, manage, and control. Outposts enables them to run workloads that need low latency access to on-premises systems locally while connecting back to the AWS GovCloud Regions for application management. They can also use Outposts and AWS Services to manage and process data that remain on premises.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-03-25T19:44:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/aws-outposts-is-now-supported-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-03-25T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts is now Supported in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now supported in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. AWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-aws-opsworks-for-chef-automate-now-supports-in-place-upgrade-to-chef-automate-2","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/aws-opsworks-for-chef-automate-now-supports-in-place-upgrade-to-chef-automate-2/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T12:58:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now perform an in-place upgrade of your Chef Automate server to Chef Automate 2 from the AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate console or the AWS CLI.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChef Automate 2 is an upgrade that makes it much easier to explore the state of your infrastructure and has an even greater emphasis on compliance features than its predecessor. Since May 2019, all newly created OpsWorks for Chef Automate servers have already been created with Chef Automate 2. It is now possible for OpsWorks customers, who on-boarded prior to May 2019, to perform an in-place upgrade of their OpsWorks server from Chef Automate to Chef Automate 2. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo initiate the in-place upgrade you can use the AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate management console. Eligible servers will show a “Start Upgrade” button at the top of the server detail page. Additionally, you can use the AWS CLI by issuing the ‘start-maintenance’ command and setting the engine attribute CHEF_MAJOR_UPGRADE to true. For examples and details about upgrade eligibility and more please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opsworks/latest/userguide/opscm-a2upgrade.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-27T18:30:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/aws-opsworks-for-chef-automate-now-supports-in-place-upgrade-to-chef-automate-2/","postDateTime":"2020-01-27T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate Now Supports In-Place Upgrade to Chef Automate 2","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now perform an in-place upgrade of your Chef Automate server to Chef Automate 2 from the AWS OpsWorks for Chef Automate console or the AWS CLI.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-aws-outposts-now-available-in-seven-new-regions-additional-countries","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/aws-outposts-now-available-in-seven-new-regions-additional-countries/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:03:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now available in the following seven new regions:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts can now be shipped and installed in three new countries Canada, Bahrain, and Singapore. It is also available in Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. AWS Outposts is ideal for workloads that need low latency access to on-premises applications or systems, local data processing, or for local data storage needs. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the new regional expansion, customers can connect to the region closest to their datacenters and on-premises facilities.  They can now deploy Outposts to support their on-premises use cases in additional country locations.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/outposts/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUser Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Overview\u003c/a\u003e.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable border\u003d\"1\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\"\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eRegion Name\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eRegion\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eCanada (Central)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eca-central-1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eEU(London)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eeu-west-2\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eEU(Paris)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eeu-west-3\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eEU(Stockholm)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eeu-north-1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eMiddle East (Bahrain)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eme-south-1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eAsia (Hong Kong)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eap-east-1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"283\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eAsia (Singapore)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd width\u003d\"282\" valign\u003d\"top\"\u003e\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003eap-southeast-1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-21T19:33:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/aws-outposts-now-available-in-seven-new-regions-additional-countries/","postDateTime":"2020-01-21T12:14:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Outposts is now available in seven new regions and additional countries","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts is now available in the following seven new regions:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-announcing-general-availability-of-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/announcing-general-availability-of-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:26:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing the general availability of AWS Outposts, a new fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. AWS Outposts is ideal for workloads that need low latency access to on-premises applications or systems, local data processing, or for local data storage needs. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can now run Amazon EC2, Amazon EBS, container-based services such as Amazon ECS and Amazon EKS, database services such as Amazon RDS on AWS Outposts, and analytics services such as Amazon EMR locally on your Outposts. You can seamlessly connect to the broad range of services and tools available in the local AWS Region such as Amazon DynamoDB, AWS CloudFormation, Amazon CloudWatch, AWS CloudTrail, Elastic BeanStalk, Cloud 9, and others to run and manage workloads on Outposts the same way as you do in the cloud today.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo order your Outpost, you can log-in to the AWS Management Console and select from a range of pre-validated Outposts configurations offering a mix of Amazon EC2 and Amazon EBS capacity that best suits your application needs and site characteristics.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts infrastructure is delivered, installed, managed, and monitored by AWS, removing the need to manually administer, upgrade, and patch your on-premises infrastructure.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStarting today, AWS Outposts can be installed and operated in the following countries: United States of America, all EU countries, Switzerland, Norway, Australia, Japan, and South Korea.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on Outposts visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;To learn more about Outposts, read our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-outposts-now-available-order-your-racks-today/\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-03T19:53:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/announcing-general-availability-of-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2019-12-03T12:26:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing General Availability of AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing the general availability of AWS Outposts, a new fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any customer datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent hybrid experience. AWS Outposts is ideal for workloads that need low latency access to on-premises applications or systems, local data processing, or for local data storage needs. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-ecs-amazon-eks-aws-app-mesh-now-support-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-ecs-amazon-eks-aws-app-mesh-now-support-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:21:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon ECS, Amazon EKS, and AWS App Mesh now support AWS Outposts, a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent hybrid experience. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS customers can now leverage Amazon ECS and EKS to run containers in customer locations using AWS Outposts for applications and datasets with latency dependencies.  By deploying on Outposts, customers can extend the AWS tooling, and performance to on-premises. AWS App Mesh can be configured to provide consistent communication control logic for services across AWS Outposts and AWS cloud to simplify hybrid application networking. Customers can centrally manage ECS, EKS, App Mesh, and their container environments both on Outposts and in the AWS cloud with the same AWS console and API framework for a unified operational model. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFind out more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ecs/\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-03T23:32:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-ecs-amazon-eks-aws-app-mesh-now-support-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2019-12-03T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon ECS, Amazon EKS, and AWS App Mesh now support AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon ECS, Amazon EKS, and AWS App Mesh now support AWS Outposts, a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, and tools to virtually any datacenter, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent hybrid experience. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ecs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ecs","description":"general:products/amazon-ecs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-app-mesh","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-app-mesh","description":"general:products/aws-app-mesh","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-emr-is-now-available-in-your-data-center-with-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-emr-is-now-available-in-your-data-center-with-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:09:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:39:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EMR is now available on AWS Outposts, allowing you to deploy open-source tools like Apache Spark and Apache Hive in your data center. Using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/emr/features/outposts/\"\u003eAmazon EMR on AWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e, you can set up, deploy, manage, and scale Apache Hadoop, Apache Hive, Apache Spark, and Presto clusters in your on-premises environments, just as you would in the cloud. Amazon EMR on AWS Outposts provides cost-efficient capacity while automating time-consuming administration tasks like infrastructure provisioning, cluster setup, configuration, or tuning, freeing you to focus on your applications.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/emr/features/outposts/\"\u003eAWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e is a fully managed service that extends AWS infrastructure, AWS services, APIs, and tools to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a consistent hybrid experience. You can use EMR on Outposts to augment on-premises processing capacity during periods of high utilization, and to process data that needs to remain on-premises for governance, compliance, or other reasons.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing AWS Outposts, you can launch EMR clusters in your data center using the same AWS Management Console, Software Development Kit (SDK), and Command Line Interface (CLI) used to launch EMR clusters in the cloud. When launching a cluster, you simply specify the subnet associated with your Outpost. EMR clusters running on an Outpost will appear in the EMR console just like clusters running in the cloud.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about EMR and Outposts, see our \u003ca\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ManagementGuide/emr-plan-outposts.html\"\u003emanagement guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-03T20:46:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-emr-is-now-available-in-your-data-center-with-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2019-12-03T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EMR is now available in your data center with AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EMR is now available on AWS Outposts, allowing you to deploy open-source tools like Apache Spark and Apache Hive in your data center. Using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/emr/features/outposts.html\"\u003eAmazon EMR on AWS Outposts\u003c/a\u003e, you can set up, deploy, manage, and scale Apache Hadoop, Apache Hive, Apache Spark, and Presto clusters in your on-premises environments, just as you would in the cloud. Amazon EMR on AWS Outposts provides cost-efficient capacity while automating time-consuming administration tasks like infrastructure provisioning, cluster setup, configuration, or tuning, freeing you to focus on your applications.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-announcing-aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/announcing-aws-outposts/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                AWS Outposts bring native AWS services, infrastructure, and operating models to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent and seamless hybrid cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                Previously, hybrid cloud solutions required you to operate different IT and development environments for on-premises and cloud, coordinate across vendors for hardware, software, and services, and maintain, update, and patch on-premises infrastructure. This creates a lot of complexity and risk with different automation, governance policies, and security controls across your environments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts remove the complexity of hybrid cloud by offering a solution that uses the same software, services, infrastructure, management tools, development, and deployment models on Outposts as you use on AWS for a seamless hybrid cloud solution. You can use the same automation, governance controls, policies, APIs, and developer tools to build and deploy modern cloud-native applications that can be deployed on-premises or in the cloud. Outposts infrastructure is fully managed, maintained, and supported by AWS, and its hardware and software components can be updated to deliver access to the latest AWS services. Outposts support workloads that remain on-premises due to low latency and local data processing needs, such as telecom virtual network functions, high-frequency trading, industrial automation, financial services, healthcare, and other applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e              AWS Outposts come in two variants: 1) VMware Cloud on AWS service that runs on AWS Outposts; 2) AWS Outposts that allow customers to run compute and storage on-premises using the same native AWS APIs used in the AWS cloud. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Outposts will be generally available in the second half of 2019. Visit the AWS Outposts \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/outposts/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/announcing-aws-outposts/","postDateTime":"2018-11-28T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing AWS Outposts","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                AWS Outposts bring native AWS services, infrastructure, and operating models to virtually any data center, co-location space, or on-premises facility for a truly consistent and seamless hybrid cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-outposts","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-outposts","description":"general:products/aws-outposts","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":102,"totalHits":102},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}